1
00:00:07,674 --> 00:00:09,301
[mic feedback]

2
00:00:09,384 --> 00:00:12,054
[host] We will reveal the results
of the Seeker Vote.

3
00:00:12,137 --> 00:00:13,805
[♪ tense music playing]

4
00:00:13,889 --> 00:00:18,727
The player who received
the most votes is...

5
00:00:20,062 --> 00:00:21,730
Kim Ddolddol.

6
00:00:22,731 --> 00:00:26,526
[chuckles] It's getting pretty annoying
to be named twice.

7
00:00:27,277 --> 00:00:29,488
[host] Based on
the final Seeker Vote results...

8
00:00:30,072 --> 00:00:33,492
[Sanghyun] Ddolddol has to be the Seeker
so that I can make it to the finals.

9
00:00:35,118 --> 00:00:38,622
[host] Your attempt to catch the Seeker

10
00:00:38,705 --> 00:00:40,332
has failed.

11
00:00:41,083 --> 00:00:43,252
-What?
-[♪ contemplative music playing]

12
00:00:43,335 --> 00:00:45,712
YOUN SANGHYUN FAILS
TO ADVANCE TO THE FINALS

13
00:00:45,796 --> 00:00:47,714
You dug your own grave, Sanghyun.

14
00:00:48,465 --> 00:00:49,716
Well done.

15
00:00:49,800 --> 00:00:51,510
[Sanghyun] What? Then, who's the Seeker?

16
00:00:53,387 --> 00:00:55,013
I was so sure it was Ddolddol.

17
00:00:55,097 --> 00:00:57,432
The Seeker must've been so happy.

18
00:00:57,516 --> 00:00:59,726
[Dail] Every prediction I make
turns out to be wrong.

19
00:00:59,810 --> 00:01:01,353
I've lost all faith in my gut here.

20
00:01:01,937 --> 00:01:04,523
[host] We will now reveal
the identity of the Seeker.

21
00:01:04,606 --> 00:01:06,608
[cheers]

22
00:01:06,692 --> 00:01:09,111
Advancing to the finals
as the Seeker is...

23
00:01:09,987 --> 00:01:11,113
[Jimin] Gosh, who could it be?

24
00:01:11,697 --> 00:01:12,698
[Joonsu] I want to know.

25
00:01:16,118 --> 00:01:17,953
-[host] Hwang Jaegyun.
-[♪ dramatic music playing]

26
00:01:18,036 --> 00:01:19,246
[Joonsu and Ddolddol exclaim]

27
00:01:19,329 --> 00:01:20,539
-[Ddolddol] Jaegyun!
-[Jaegyun chuckles]

28
00:01:22,457 --> 00:01:25,252
[Sanghyun groans]

29
00:01:25,961 --> 00:01:27,004
[Sanghyun] So it was Jaegyun.

30
00:01:30,048 --> 00:01:31,133
[sighs]

31
00:01:31,758 --> 00:01:34,678
When we were talking outside,
he said it really wasn't him.

32
00:01:34,761 --> 00:01:38,181
I thought Jaegyun was one person
I could trust not to lie to me.

33
00:01:38,265 --> 00:01:40,642
But I got blindsided by someone I trusted.

34
00:01:41,435 --> 00:01:46,023
[ZZONE] I was so shocked,
and I felt so betrayed.

35
00:01:47,190 --> 00:01:51,695
[Jimin] Jaegyun
is especially terrible at lying.

36
00:01:51,778 --> 00:01:55,198
He's like a sweet, innocent
neighborhood-uncle kind of guy.

37
00:01:55,282 --> 00:01:59,119
But that uncle pulled it off?
I was a little jealous.

38
00:01:59,745 --> 00:02:03,874
From Sanghyun's perspective,
it must've been really frustrating.

39
00:02:05,250 --> 00:02:06,626
[Sanghyun] It was quite shocking.

40
00:02:06,710 --> 00:02:09,463
I thought I did well,
but now I'm going to the Death Match.

41
00:02:10,047 --> 00:02:13,967
[Jaegyun] I felt really good.
I'd actually managed to fool them.

42
00:02:14,509 --> 00:02:17,554
THE NIGHT BEFORE

43
00:02:18,138 --> 00:02:21,058
[host] Now, we will select a new Seeker.

44
00:02:21,141 --> 00:02:22,351
[♪ ominous music playing]

45
00:02:22,434 --> 00:02:24,770
Please enter the Dealer Room
one at a time.

46
00:02:27,773 --> 00:02:31,443
[dealer] Mr. Hwang Jaegyun, please select
a card to determine the Seeker.

47
00:02:39,201 --> 00:02:41,536
Mr. Hwang Jaegyun,
you have become the Seeker.

48
00:02:41,620 --> 00:02:44,289
[Jaegyun] When I suddenly heard,
"You're the Seeker," I thought...

49
00:02:48,627 --> 00:02:50,587
"This is going to be really fun."

50
00:02:53,215 --> 00:02:55,217
ANOTHER SECRET PASSAGE

51
00:02:55,300 --> 00:02:56,968
HIDDEN IN THEIR LODGINGS

52
00:02:57,719 --> 00:03:01,932
I heard there was a Seeker Room
in the Dining Room.

53
00:03:02,516 --> 00:03:05,185
WHILE THE OTHER PLAYERS
PLAN THEIR STRATEGY

54
00:03:05,852 --> 00:03:08,689
I snuck in at night
when no one was around.

55
00:03:10,023 --> 00:03:11,316
I opened the painting,

56
00:03:13,193 --> 00:03:14,945
went through the secret passage...

57
00:03:18,156 --> 00:03:20,075
and found the Seeker Room.

58
00:03:22,661 --> 00:03:25,122
I never would've guessed
there was a room like this.

59
00:03:25,205 --> 00:03:26,206
ANOTHER SEEKER ROOM

60
00:03:31,253 --> 00:03:32,421
[sighs heavily]

61
00:03:32,504 --> 00:03:33,547
MAIN MATCH "RAINBOW CATCH"

62
00:03:33,630 --> 00:03:37,384
The Seeker's mission was to be
every color at least once.

63
00:03:38,260 --> 00:03:40,095
Was that even possible?

64
00:03:40,178 --> 00:03:42,514
How did you do that?
That must've been so hard.

65
00:03:43,181 --> 00:03:46,143
I think that was
the hardest mission so far.

66
00:03:46,226 --> 00:03:47,727
Gosh, he did all that?

67
00:03:47,811 --> 00:03:51,648
So it was good to get tagged a lot
and to start as a White Card.

68
00:03:51,731 --> 00:03:53,859
No, if I started as a White Card

69
00:03:53,942 --> 00:03:55,694
and couldn't tag anyone
within five minutes,

70
00:03:55,777 --> 00:03:57,821
I'd be stuck here
and unable to do anything.

71
00:03:57,904 --> 00:03:59,448
Wow, that's unbelievable.

72
00:04:00,115 --> 00:04:02,701
That might've been harder
than coming in first or second.

73
00:04:02,784 --> 00:04:04,286
He had to get the Black Card too.

74
00:04:04,369 --> 00:04:05,829
Jaegyun is good.

75
00:04:05,912 --> 00:04:08,248
I thought he played the game
incredibly well.

76
00:04:08,331 --> 00:04:11,126
Just like his personality,
his play was decisive and bold.

77
00:04:11,209 --> 00:04:13,879
I'd say he played it perfectly
as the Seeker.

78
00:04:13,962 --> 00:04:16,840
[Jaegyun] I thought,
"What do you mean 'black'?"

79
00:04:16,923 --> 00:04:19,176
"What does that color even do?"

80
00:04:19,259 --> 00:04:21,803
Since I didn't have any prior information,

81
00:04:21,887 --> 00:04:25,182
I started running to find it
as soon as the game started.

82
00:04:25,265 --> 00:04:27,225
[sighs, mumbles]

83
00:04:28,560 --> 00:04:29,895
Where is it?

84
00:04:31,688 --> 00:04:33,482
I checked the map

85
00:04:33,565 --> 00:04:36,109
and the basement seemed suspicious,
so I went down there.

86
00:04:41,948 --> 00:04:43,533
The Black Card was in the basement

87
00:04:43,617 --> 00:04:44,701
FOUND IT WITH HORSEKING

88
00:04:44,785 --> 00:04:47,120
-I knew it had to be part of the mission.
-[♪ contemplative music playing]

89
00:04:48,079 --> 00:04:53,126
I absolutely needed this.
But I didn't know how to bring that up.

90
00:04:53,210 --> 00:04:54,920
"What should I tell him so I can use it?"

91
00:04:55,003 --> 00:04:57,088
That's what I kept thinking about.

92
00:05:02,469 --> 00:05:03,845
Do you want to hold onto the card?

93
00:05:05,472 --> 00:05:06,681
Okay, I'll hold onto it.

94
00:05:07,307 --> 00:05:10,143
So I was like, "Yes! Thank you,"
and put it in my pocket.

95
00:05:10,227 --> 00:05:14,314
So in the beginning,
I started with the Blue Card.

96
00:05:14,397 --> 00:05:16,983
-[♪ exciting music playing]
-And I found the color cards first.

97
00:05:17,067 --> 00:05:20,946
No matter what color I found,
I thought it would work in my favor more

98
00:05:21,029 --> 00:05:24,825
to make the secondary colors first,
like green, orange, and purple.

99
00:05:24,908 --> 00:05:27,244
JAEGYUN WENT AFTER
THE SECONDARY COLORS FIRST

100
00:05:27,327 --> 00:05:28,829
I'll change my card to green.

101
00:05:29,663 --> 00:05:32,290
[dealer] Mr. Hwang Jaegyun,
your color has been changed to green.

102
00:05:33,375 --> 00:05:34,793
[Jaegyun] I spotted Joonsu right away,

103
00:05:34,876 --> 00:05:37,087
and he came at me saying,
"I'm a White Card."

104
00:05:38,046 --> 00:05:42,843
I thought I needed to get tagged then
and quickly get rid of the white card.

105
00:05:42,926 --> 00:05:46,096
But if I got caught too easily,
that would raise suspicions,

106
00:05:46,179 --> 00:05:47,848
so I dragged out the standoff.

107
00:05:49,307 --> 00:05:51,476
FEIGNING ESCAPE,
JAEGYUN LETS HIMSELF GET CAUGHT

108
00:05:52,227 --> 00:05:54,312
EASILY TAKES CARE OF THE WHITE CARD

109
00:05:54,396 --> 00:05:57,774
I started walking around
and Junseo appeared in front of me.

110
00:05:57,858 --> 00:05:59,860
Luckily, his card was orange.

111
00:06:01,778 --> 00:06:04,614
I thought, "Things are going
pretty smoothly for me."

112
00:06:04,698 --> 00:06:06,283
I'm sorry, man. I have to.

113
00:06:06,366 --> 00:06:07,617
ALL CLEARED IN ROUND 1

114
00:06:08,410 --> 00:06:09,953
SOMEONE HAS CHANGED HWANG JAEGYUN'S COLOR

115
00:06:10,036 --> 00:06:11,079
PLEASE GO TO THE DEALER ROOM NOW

116
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:13,748
[dealer]
Your color has been changed to purple.

117
00:06:13,832 --> 00:06:16,001
[Jaegyun] They told me my color
had changed to purple.

118
00:06:16,084 --> 00:06:17,502
I hadn't even used my card though.

119
00:06:17,586 --> 00:06:20,630
From then on, I felt pretty sure

120
00:06:20,714 --> 00:06:22,716
that I wouldn't be caught
as the Seeker today.

121
00:06:23,383 --> 00:06:24,718
I'll change my card to yellow.

122
00:06:26,386 --> 00:06:28,096
[dealer]
We will change your card color to yellow.

123
00:06:28,179 --> 00:06:29,431
CLEARED ALL THE COLOR CARDS

124
00:06:29,514 --> 00:06:33,977
Now, the last thing was the Black Card
and how I was going to use it.

125
00:06:34,060 --> 00:06:35,729
That's all I was focusing on.

126
00:06:37,314 --> 00:06:38,940
I'm minus 10 points anyway.

127
00:06:39,941 --> 00:06:41,401
[Jaegyun] Horseking seemed like

128
00:06:41,484 --> 00:06:44,195
he'd pretty much given up
on first or second place.

129
00:06:44,279 --> 00:06:48,325
I asked if I could use the Black Card
at the end, and he said...

130
00:06:48,950 --> 00:06:50,243
Sure, go ahead.

131
00:06:52,037 --> 00:06:53,913
[Jaegyun] And I thought,
"This is perfect."

132
00:06:53,997 --> 00:06:56,291
HWANG JAEGYUN EVEN CLEARS THE BLACK CARD

133
00:06:56,374 --> 00:06:58,376
I successfully completed
the Seeker mission,

134
00:06:58,460 --> 00:07:00,462
and everyone started suspecting Ddolddol,

135
00:07:00,545 --> 00:07:04,591
so I quietly helped spread that suspicion.

136
00:07:04,674 --> 00:07:06,051
But how could Ddolddol tag Joonsu?

137
00:07:06,134 --> 00:07:08,470
[Horseking] Exactly, so I think
he used the Black Card.

138
00:07:08,553 --> 00:07:11,014
If there's a Seeker perk,
that might be it.

139
00:07:11,097 --> 00:07:14,768
I would ask, "I think Ddolddol
is the Seeker. What do you think?"

140
00:07:14,851 --> 00:07:16,645
I'm just suspicious of him.

141
00:07:16,728 --> 00:07:18,355
-[Ddolddol] You think I'm the Seeker?
-Yeah. [chuckles]

142
00:07:18,438 --> 00:07:20,231
[Jaegyun] He said,

143
00:07:20,315 --> 00:07:22,609
"Kim Ddolddol has changed
Hwang Jaegyun's color to purple."

144
00:07:22,692 --> 00:07:24,277
[ZZONE] I think Ddolddol is the Seeker.

145
00:07:24,361 --> 00:07:25,737
I think it worked really well.

146
00:07:25,820 --> 00:07:27,238
JAEGYUN DID HIS MISSION PERFECTLY

147
00:07:27,822 --> 00:07:31,117
[host] We will announce
the first two finalists.

148
00:07:31,201 --> 00:07:35,163
-[♪ dramatic music playing]
-The Main Match winner, Yang Dail,

149
00:07:35,246 --> 00:07:39,668
and the Seeker who avoided capture
in the Seeker Vote, Hwang Jaegyun,

150
00:07:39,751 --> 00:07:42,504
have secured their spots in the final.

151
00:07:42,587 --> 00:07:46,675
-[♪ upbeat music playing]
-Finalists Yang Dail and Hwang Jaegyun

152
00:07:46,758 --> 00:07:48,051
may leave the area.

153
00:07:48,635 --> 00:07:52,555
[Jaegyun] Before I knew it,
I was in the finals.

154
00:07:52,639 --> 00:07:55,475
That really made me want to win.

155
00:08:01,523 --> 00:08:03,525
[♪ ominous music playing]

156
00:08:17,747 --> 00:08:22,043
[host] We will now begin
the final Death Match of Deadly Tag.

157
00:08:22,127 --> 00:08:27,465
Only three survivors from this Death Match
will advance to the finals.

158
00:08:27,549 --> 00:08:31,094
-A lot of people are going home today.
-Four people are getting eliminated?

159
00:08:31,177 --> 00:08:33,012
[sighs]

160
00:08:33,596 --> 00:08:36,558
[Jimin] The thought of facing
these six in the Death Match...

161
00:08:36,641 --> 00:08:39,894
[Horseking] That was the first time
I really thought I might get eliminated.

162
00:08:39,978 --> 00:08:42,522
[Junseo] I didn't want
to go home like this.

163
00:08:43,606 --> 00:08:46,151
[Sanghyun] I just had to survive
the Death Match

164
00:08:46,234 --> 00:08:47,694
and make it to the final.

165
00:08:47,777 --> 00:08:51,531
[Ddolddol] I've always survived,
so I think I can make it to the final.

166
00:08:52,073 --> 00:08:53,616
[host] The final Death Match

167
00:08:54,993 --> 00:08:57,120
is "Dystopia."

168
00:08:57,203 --> 00:08:58,246
-[♪ dramatic music playing]
-"Dystopia"?

169
00:08:58,955 --> 00:09:01,833
[host] In this game, players use
their Character Cards

170
00:09:01,916 --> 00:09:05,128
to battle each other and earn points.

171
00:09:05,211 --> 00:09:09,466
Every player starts with a set
of Character Cards, one Weapon Card,

172
00:09:09,549 --> 00:09:11,885
and 10 coins.

173
00:09:13,011 --> 00:09:16,139
The Character Cards
are Commander, Soldier, Citizen,

174
00:09:16,222 --> 00:09:18,600
Slave, and Mutant.

175
00:09:18,683 --> 00:09:20,226
Each Character Card

176
00:09:20,310 --> 00:09:24,314
has different attack and defense stats.

177
00:09:25,815 --> 00:09:28,526
Here is how battles work.

178
00:09:28,610 --> 00:09:30,653
The player who makes a tag
becomes the Attacker,

179
00:09:30,737 --> 00:09:33,239
while the tagged player
becomes the Defender.

180
00:09:33,323 --> 00:09:36,242
Each player secretly submits
their Character Card.

181
00:09:36,326 --> 00:09:38,787
The Attacker wins
if their attack stat meets or exceeds

182
00:09:38,870 --> 00:09:40,288
the opponent's defense stat.

183
00:09:41,247 --> 00:09:44,501
However, if the Attacker plays
a Commander card

184
00:09:44,584 --> 00:09:46,836
-and the Defender plays a Slave card,
-[♪ upbeat music playing]

185
00:09:47,462 --> 00:09:50,590
the Defender wins
regardless of their stats.

186
00:09:51,174 --> 00:09:54,636
-So, the Attacker wins even in ties.
-Yes, but they can lose due to matchups.

187
00:09:54,719 --> 00:09:56,471
-Regardless of stats.
-There are matchups?

188
00:09:56,554 --> 00:09:59,015
[host] At this point,
players can equip items

189
00:09:59,099 --> 00:10:01,518
on Character Cards with Weapon Cards.

190
00:10:01,601 --> 00:10:05,480
There are three types of Weapon Cards.
Attack, Defense, and Special.

191
00:10:06,606 --> 00:10:10,652
Attack cards increase
a character's base attack power,

192
00:10:10,735 --> 00:10:14,197
while the Defense cards
boost their defense.

193
00:10:14,280 --> 00:10:18,827
Special cards activate
during battle or in specific situations.

194
00:10:20,036 --> 00:10:23,414
Any Weapon Card used in battle
is immediately discarded.

195
00:10:23,498 --> 00:10:26,000
From Round 2 onwards,
the losing player in a battle

196
00:10:26,084 --> 00:10:29,003
will also lose their Character Card.

197
00:10:29,087 --> 00:10:32,340
In addition,
the winner will earn one point,

198
00:10:32,423 --> 00:10:35,718
while the loser will lose one point.

199
00:10:38,346 --> 00:10:39,472
It's basically an RPG.

200
00:10:39,556 --> 00:10:43,393
[host] In the chase area, there are Stores
on the second floor and in the basement.

201
00:10:44,394 --> 00:10:47,772
All item cards
can be purchased from Stores.

202
00:10:47,856 --> 00:10:51,109
Each item has its own price
and purchase window.

203
00:10:51,985 --> 00:10:56,030
Coins are scattered throughout the area
and can be used to buy items.

204
00:10:56,114 --> 00:10:57,574
If you run out of coins,

205
00:10:57,657 --> 00:11:01,244
you can also sell Character Cards
at Stores to earn more.

206
00:11:02,412 --> 00:11:03,413
This sounds fun.

207
00:11:04,747 --> 00:11:06,916
[host] The game consists of two rounds.

208
00:11:07,000 --> 00:11:10,962
Round 1 will last for 40 minutes,
and Round 2 will last for 60 minutes.

209
00:11:11,045 --> 00:11:17,010
When the final round ends,
only the top three players will survive.

210
00:11:17,093 --> 00:11:20,054
This is like an RPG-style card game.

211
00:11:20,138 --> 00:11:23,183
I got this. This is my specialty.

212
00:11:23,266 --> 00:11:25,351
-[♪ rock music playing]
-I'm a huge RPG fan.

213
00:11:25,435 --> 00:11:28,021
When I heard the rules,
I knew I could do well.

214
00:11:28,980 --> 00:11:31,816
Since everyone starts with the same cards,

215
00:11:33,026 --> 00:11:36,905
this is a game I can win
simply by playing my best.

216
00:11:36,988 --> 00:11:38,198
[mic feedback]

217
00:11:38,281 --> 00:11:39,282
[ZZONE sighs]

218
00:11:39,365 --> 00:11:42,452
[host]
We will begin Round 1 of "Dystopia."

219
00:11:42,535 --> 00:11:44,078
[Joonsu whoops]

220
00:11:44,162 --> 00:11:46,414
Yuk Junseo, please go
to the VIP Dining Room

221
00:11:46,497 --> 00:11:48,041
and collect your cards and coin pouch.

222
00:11:48,124 --> 00:11:50,168
ALL GET 10 COINS
AND 1 DEFENSE OR ATTACK CARD

223
00:11:50,251 --> 00:11:51,461
[dealer] Mr. Yuk Junseo,

224
00:11:52,086 --> 00:11:55,590
you may randomly select
one of these cards.

225
00:11:55,673 --> 00:11:56,674
Please choose.

226
00:11:57,550 --> 00:11:59,552
YUK JUNSEO
SHIELD

227
00:11:59,636 --> 00:12:01,012
This one!

228
00:12:01,095 --> 00:12:02,138
WRENCH
BASIC ATTACK CARD

229
00:12:04,182 --> 00:12:05,642
YOUN SANGHYUN & HORSEKING
WRENCH

230
00:12:06,392 --> 00:12:08,102
PARK JIMIN
SHIELD

231
00:12:09,020 --> 00:12:11,064
I got the Shield card first,

232
00:12:11,147 --> 00:12:13,566
so I decided to go all-in on defense.

233
00:12:13,650 --> 00:12:15,193
ZZONE
SHIELD

234
00:12:15,276 --> 00:12:17,028
[ZZONE] Luckily, I drew a Defense card.

235
00:12:17,111 --> 00:12:19,072
Since I'm more likely to get tagged,

236
00:12:19,155 --> 00:12:22,200
I figured it'd be best to focus
entirely on defense.

237
00:12:22,283 --> 00:12:25,662
Since the Attacker wins if the attack
and defense stats are tied...

238
00:12:25,745 --> 00:12:28,248
[Ddolddol]
When I tag someone, I become the Attacker

239
00:12:28,331 --> 00:12:30,250
and they become the Defender,

240
00:12:30,333 --> 00:12:32,168
so I decided to go all-in on attacking.

241
00:12:32,252 --> 00:12:33,544
...I'll go all-in on attacking.

242
00:12:33,628 --> 00:12:34,754
And I'll hunt everyone down.

243
00:12:34,837 --> 00:12:36,464
And I'll go around tagging people.

244
00:12:36,547 --> 00:12:39,467
SANGHYUN, HORSEKING, DDOLDDOL
JUNSEO, JIMIN, JOONSU, ZZONE

245
00:12:39,550 --> 00:12:42,679
PLAYER WEAPON SELECTION COMPLETE

246
00:12:43,972 --> 00:12:46,140
[♪ exciting rock music playing]

247
00:12:47,642 --> 00:12:51,312
[host] We will now begin Round 1's chase.

248
00:12:56,693 --> 00:12:57,694
2 COINS

249
00:12:58,736 --> 00:12:59,737
2 COINS

250
00:13:03,324 --> 00:13:04,325
1 COIN

251
00:13:04,409 --> 00:13:07,704
[ZZONE] Since the best chance
to find coins would be during Round 1,

252
00:13:07,787 --> 00:13:10,832
I figured I needed to collect
as many coins as possible.

253
00:13:11,457 --> 00:13:13,293
[Sanghyun] My strategy
was to stock up on coins,

254
00:13:13,376 --> 00:13:15,169
play it safe by purchasing items,

255
00:13:15,253 --> 00:13:18,131
and make sure
that I face opponents aggressively.

256
00:13:20,967 --> 00:13:24,971
PLAYERS FOCUS ON COLLECTING COINS
EVEN WHEN THEY CROSS PATHS

257
00:13:30,184 --> 00:13:32,854
[Jimin] There was this locked box.

258
00:13:32,937 --> 00:13:34,355
[♪ music continues]

259
00:13:39,027 --> 00:13:43,489
PLAYERS BEGIN FINDING PUZZLE BOXES

260
00:13:53,374 --> 00:13:55,585
[Jimin]
I first multiplied the number pairs.

261
00:13:55,668 --> 00:13:58,379
Three times three is nine.
Four times five is twenty.

262
00:14:00,089 --> 00:14:03,342
Then I added the first number in each,
and they matched perfectly.

263
00:14:05,011 --> 00:14:07,013
[whispers] Seven times seven
is forty-nine.

264
00:14:07,096 --> 00:14:08,598
That makes 49.

265
00:14:08,681 --> 00:14:12,060
Then, 49 plus 7 is 56.

266
00:14:12,143 --> 00:14:15,396
And 88... 88...

267
00:14:16,773 --> 00:14:17,815
Okay.

268
00:14:22,361 --> 00:14:23,362
10 COINS

269
00:14:29,327 --> 00:14:31,579
[Junseo] I looked at the first line
in the puzzle.

270
00:14:34,373 --> 00:14:35,917
If you multiply the two numbers,

271
00:14:36,000 --> 00:14:38,419
you get the first two numbers
in the answer.

272
00:14:38,503 --> 00:14:41,756
Adding the two numbers gives you
the next two numbers in the answer,

273
00:14:41,839 --> 00:14:46,094
and the difference of the two numbers
give you the last number in the answer.

274
00:14:49,847 --> 00:14:51,349
That's 4, 1, 0...

275
00:14:56,771 --> 00:14:58,940
[Ddolddol] All the areas I had hidden in
during the Main Match

276
00:14:59,023 --> 00:15:01,150
were ones I'd searched before.

277
00:15:01,234 --> 00:15:04,403
And sure enough,
there were coins all over these places.

278
00:15:04,487 --> 00:15:09,534
I was so good at finding them.
I must've found over 50 coins.

279
00:15:09,617 --> 00:15:12,662
Maybe 70 or 80?
Yeah, I think I found around 80.

280
00:15:12,745 --> 00:15:14,622
1. SANGHYUN, 2. DDOLDDOL,
3. JOONSU, 4 .JIMIN

281
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:16,124
5. HORSEKING, 6. JUNSEO, 7. ZZONE

282
00:15:16,207 --> 00:15:18,668
10 STARTING COINS

283
00:15:18,751 --> 00:15:20,670
7. ZZONE

284
00:15:20,753 --> 00:15:22,255
[♪ quirky music playing]

285
00:15:22,338 --> 00:15:23,589
They've already looked everywhere.

286
00:15:25,424 --> 00:15:27,593
Where are they?

287
00:15:29,137 --> 00:15:31,305
What the heck? A math question?

288
00:15:31,889 --> 00:15:34,433
FAILS TO FIND COINS
AFTER GETTING STUCK ON THE PUZZLE

289
00:15:38,396 --> 00:15:39,397
[Horseking] Okay.

290
00:15:39,480 --> 00:15:43,776
SHE DOESN'T SEARCH CAREFULLY,
SO FAILS TO FIND COINS

291
00:15:43,860 --> 00:15:45,153
[Ddolddol] Shit.

292
00:15:46,154 --> 00:15:47,655
[ZZONE whispering] They opened everything.

293
00:15:49,323 --> 00:15:51,951
I think I found around 25.

294
00:15:52,034 --> 00:15:55,204
[whispering] I think they've found
all of them. This is bad.

295
00:15:55,288 --> 00:15:58,666
I think I'll need to focus more
on the battle of wits instead.

296
00:16:01,043 --> 00:16:03,880
ZZONE RANKS LAST IN COINS

297
00:16:06,883 --> 00:16:07,967
[Horseking] Did you find some coins?

298
00:16:08,050 --> 00:16:09,427
-[ZZONE] Sorry?
-[Horseking] Did you find some coins?

299
00:16:09,510 --> 00:16:10,511
[ZZONE] I'm trying to.

300
00:16:10,595 --> 00:16:11,929
-[Horseking] What?
-[ZZONE] Are you going to tag me?

301
00:16:12,013 --> 00:16:13,222
Yeah, I'm about to.

302
00:16:13,306 --> 00:16:16,517
It's all about having the advantage.
I thought I could definitely win.

303
00:16:16,601 --> 00:16:18,895
-Well, let's give it a try.
-[Horseking] Let's give it a try.

304
00:16:19,770 --> 00:16:21,063
[host] Tag confirmed.

305
00:16:21,147 --> 00:16:22,190
HORSEKING TAGS ZZONE

306
00:16:22,273 --> 00:16:24,150
-I was really pleased.
-[♪ exciting music playing]

307
00:16:24,233 --> 00:16:26,527
Since you don't lose
your Character Card in Round 1,

308
00:16:26,611 --> 00:16:28,738
I wanted to get into a battle early on

309
00:16:28,821 --> 00:16:32,241
to see what strategies would work best
against the other players later on.

310
00:16:32,325 --> 00:16:33,743
I couldn't wait to test things out.

311
00:16:34,911 --> 00:16:39,457
[dealer] Attacker, please place
your Attack card face down first.

312
00:16:40,208 --> 00:16:41,209
Okay.

313
00:16:42,585 --> 00:16:43,961
[dealer] As the Defender, Ms. ZZONE...

314
00:16:44,045 --> 00:16:46,130
-Yes.
-...please submit your card as well.

315
00:16:47,632 --> 00:16:50,551
[ZZONE] It seemed like he'd play
his Commander card right from the start.

316
00:16:50,635 --> 00:16:52,220
Once you both think you have Kings,

317
00:16:52,303 --> 00:16:54,055
you play the Joker with a warrior's heart.

318
00:16:54,138 --> 00:16:57,975
HORSEKING WAS ALWAYS ON THE OFFENSIVE

319
00:16:58,059 --> 00:17:01,604
[ZZONE] I thought I had to win this
by strengthening my Defense cards.

320
00:17:02,521 --> 00:17:05,358
[Horseking] In any case, the Attacker
has the advantage in this game.

321
00:17:08,653 --> 00:17:09,779
[ZZONE sighs]

322
00:17:09,862 --> 00:17:12,073
[dealer]
We will check both players' cards.

323
00:17:13,407 --> 00:17:15,409
MUTANT

324
00:17:15,493 --> 00:17:16,702
SHIELD
BASIC DEFENSE CARD

325
00:17:17,203 --> 00:17:19,038
Mutant has a defense stat of 4

326
00:17:19,121 --> 00:17:21,165
and Shield has a defense stat of 1

327
00:17:21,249 --> 00:17:23,209
for a total defense of 5.

328
00:17:24,043 --> 00:17:27,421
ZZONE USED HIGHEST-DEFENSE STAT
FROM MUTANT CARD AND A SHIELD

329
00:17:27,505 --> 00:17:29,674
Now, we will reveal Horseking's card.

330
00:17:30,258 --> 00:17:31,676
WRENCH
BASIC ATTACK CARD

331
00:17:36,097 --> 00:17:37,390
SOLDIER

332
00:17:39,100 --> 00:17:40,309
-[♪ upbeat music playing]
-A Wrench for 1 Attack

333
00:17:40,393 --> 00:17:41,561
another Wrench for 1 Attack,

334
00:17:41,644 --> 00:17:42,979
and a Soldier for 3 Attack.

335
00:17:43,062 --> 00:17:45,731
Horseking's total attack power is 5.

336
00:17:47,567 --> 00:17:50,361
ZZONE AND HORSEKING BOTH HAVE
A TOTAL OF 5 POINTS FOR A TIE

337
00:17:50,444 --> 00:17:52,071
The Attacker, Horseking, wins.

338
00:17:52,154 --> 00:17:53,281
ATTACKER WINS IN EVENT OF A TIE

339
00:17:53,364 --> 00:17:55,241
-You used the advantage.
-[laughs]

340
00:17:55,575 --> 00:18:00,204
As long as my opponents don't stop by
the Store, I can't lose. The reason is...

341
00:18:00,788 --> 00:18:03,416
RIGHT AFTER THE ROUND BEGAN
2 COINS

342
00:18:03,499 --> 00:18:06,377
I started picking up coins
little by little from the start.

343
00:18:07,878 --> 00:18:11,132
And my route naturally took me
toward the Store.

344
00:18:11,215 --> 00:18:12,216
STORE 1

345
00:18:12,300 --> 00:18:14,218
2ND-FLOOR STORE

346
00:18:15,428 --> 00:18:17,930
HORSEKING VISITS STORE
AFTER ONLY 3 MINUTES AND 30 SECONDS

347
00:18:19,473 --> 00:18:22,351
WEAPON CARDS
CURRENTLY AVAILABLE FOR PURCHASE

348
00:18:22,435 --> 00:18:24,395
I started thinking outside the box.

349
00:18:24,478 --> 00:18:26,564
Everyone's so obsessed
with finding coins now.

350
00:18:26,647 --> 00:18:29,317
Even if they have a Defense card,
they probably only have one.

351
00:18:29,400 --> 00:18:32,612
When attack and defense stats tie,
the Attacker always wins.

352
00:18:32,695 --> 00:18:36,407
If I rushed over to buy an Attack card
and made a combination that couldn't lose,

353
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:39,577
I suddenly realized I'd win for sure
just by tagging anyone.

354
00:18:40,161 --> 00:18:41,412
Give me one Wrench, please.

355
00:18:41,495 --> 00:18:44,999
HORSEKING BUYS AN ATTACK CARD
WITHOUT HESITATION

356
00:18:45,082 --> 00:18:47,251
Even if I go against
the highest possible defense,

357
00:18:47,335 --> 00:18:48,961
it would only be the Mutant's 4.

358
00:18:49,045 --> 00:18:50,921
Plus 1 from a Shield would make that 5.

359
00:18:51,005 --> 00:18:54,258
But since there's the variable
where the Slave card beats the Commander,

360
00:18:55,134 --> 00:18:57,428
I decided not to play the Commander.

361
00:18:58,429 --> 00:19:02,350
So, I used the Soldier's 3 attack points,
the 1 point from the card I started with,

362
00:19:02,433 --> 00:19:05,770
and the 1-point card I bought
at the Store to make it 5.

363
00:19:06,354 --> 00:19:10,900
Even if it became a 5-to-5 tie,
the Attacker gets the advantage,

364
00:19:10,983 --> 00:19:13,694
so there was no way I could lose.

365
00:19:13,778 --> 00:19:16,405
HORSEKING WINS AND EARNS 1 POINT

366
00:19:18,074 --> 00:19:19,492
STRAIGHT BACK TO THE STORE

367
00:19:20,826 --> 00:19:22,745
Give me two Wrenches, please.

368
00:19:25,081 --> 00:19:27,458
HORSEKING SPOTS DDOLDDOL BUSILY SEARCHING

369
00:19:30,294 --> 00:19:31,837
-Let's play a game.
-[Ddolddol sighs]

370
00:19:31,921 --> 00:19:33,506
-[host] Tag confirmed.
-Are you the Attacker?

371
00:19:33,589 --> 00:19:34,590
Yes.

372
00:19:39,261 --> 00:19:42,348
[dealer] Mr. Kim Ddolddol,
please place your Defense card.

373
00:19:43,641 --> 00:19:44,850
HORSEKING DEFEATS DDOLDDOL 5 TO 4

374
00:19:44,934 --> 00:19:46,435
Horseking wins.

375
00:19:47,770 --> 00:19:49,814
[Horseking] I earned
those first two points right away.

376
00:19:49,897 --> 00:19:52,358
While everyone else was busy
collecting coins,

377
00:19:52,441 --> 00:19:55,403
I was already racking up points.

378
00:19:55,486 --> 00:19:57,446
That's what the game is really all about.

379
00:19:57,530 --> 00:20:00,074
HORSEKING IS BACK AT THE STORE

380
00:20:00,658 --> 00:20:03,119
NEWLY RELEASED CARDS AFTER 15 MINUTES

381
00:20:03,202 --> 00:20:06,872
[host] Newly released cards
can provide additional benefits

382
00:20:06,956 --> 00:20:08,999
when certain special conditions are met.

383
00:20:09,083 --> 00:20:11,127
[♪ upbeat music playing]

384
00:20:11,210 --> 00:20:13,462
[Horseking] I need to start
picking up coins now.

385
00:20:13,546 --> 00:20:17,675
For now, I'll go with the Shield
and Barricade cards for 11 coins.

386
00:20:18,509 --> 00:20:19,802
I bought some Defense cards

387
00:20:19,885 --> 00:20:22,096
because someone could tag me
while I'm searching.

388
00:20:24,890 --> 00:20:28,728
Where are they? Nice. Nice!

389
00:20:28,811 --> 00:20:30,896
If I take my time, I bet I'll find a lot.

390
00:20:33,023 --> 00:20:36,485
HORSEKING ALSO FINDS A PUZZLE BOX

391
00:20:37,069 --> 00:20:40,364
OPENS IT WITH FORCE

392
00:20:42,450 --> 00:20:44,326
It's all adding up little by little.

393
00:20:44,410 --> 00:20:48,122
FOCUSING ON FINDING COINS
WITH FAITH IN HIS DEFENSE CARDS

394
00:20:52,209 --> 00:20:53,669
-Hi.
-[Sanghyun] Are you going to tag me?

395
00:20:53,753 --> 00:20:54,754
[Horseking] Nope.

396
00:20:57,882 --> 00:21:00,217
Are they all gone?
Do I need to go to the third floor?

397
00:21:05,014 --> 00:21:07,308
-Have you found a lot?
-[Sanghyun] Where's the Store?

398
00:21:07,391 --> 00:21:08,476
[Horseking] What?

399
00:21:09,268 --> 00:21:10,686
[host] Tag confirmed.

400
00:21:11,187 --> 00:21:12,938
[Horseking] Okay, let's do it.
I've already done two.

401
00:21:13,022 --> 00:21:16,150
I had a feeling Horseking
would play aggressively.

402
00:21:16,233 --> 00:21:18,068
I thought he wouldn't have
many Defense cards.

403
00:21:18,152 --> 00:21:21,071
But I took all of that into account.

404
00:21:21,155 --> 00:21:24,116
I'll go with the Shield
and Barricade cards for 11 coins.

405
00:21:24,200 --> 00:21:25,993
HORSEKING PREPARED TO BE TAGGED IN ADVANCE

406
00:21:26,076 --> 00:21:27,453
It was actually better for me.

407
00:21:27,536 --> 00:21:29,038
I thought, "What a lucky break,"

408
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:30,664
and used it to my advantage.

409
00:21:31,290 --> 00:21:33,250
[Sanghyun] I did briefly wonder
if he had any Defense cards.

410
00:21:35,294 --> 00:21:36,629
-This is fun.
-It really is.

411
00:21:36,712 --> 00:21:37,713
This is fun.

412
00:21:37,797 --> 00:21:38,964
[Sanghyun] I was confident I could win.

413
00:21:41,008 --> 00:21:43,052
[dealer] We will check the battle results.

414
00:21:44,804 --> 00:21:48,599
HORSEKING'S CARDS
MUTANT 4, SHIELD 1, BARRICADE 3

415
00:21:48,682 --> 00:21:51,769
[Horseking] If you play a Barricade
with a Shield, it gets an extra point.

416
00:21:52,436 --> 00:21:54,438
So, my defense was 9.

417
00:21:55,523 --> 00:21:56,774
[dealer] Here are the battle results.

418
00:21:58,025 --> 00:21:59,735
Youn Sanghyun wins.

419
00:21:59,819 --> 00:22:00,820
-Thank you.
-[♪ upbeat rock music playing]

420
00:22:00,903 --> 00:22:02,404
HORSEKING'S CARDS
TOTAL 9 POINTS

421
00:22:02,488 --> 00:22:04,865
SANGHYUN'S CARDS
SOLDIER 3, PISTOL 3, PISTOL 3

422
00:22:04,949 --> 00:22:07,284
9 TO 9 TIE GOES TO ATTACKER
YOUN SANGHYUN WINS

423
00:22:09,245 --> 00:22:10,246
[Horseking] How did he do that?

424
00:22:10,329 --> 00:22:11,580
It's a tie.

425
00:22:11,664 --> 00:22:13,666
[Sanghyun] I was 100% sure
I was going to win.

426
00:22:14,458 --> 00:22:17,211
I saw the announcement
that Horseking tagged two people.

427
00:22:17,294 --> 00:22:20,339
That made me think,
"Horseking probably has a point total."

428
00:22:20,422 --> 00:22:22,424
"But he probably
doesn't have many cards."`

429
00:22:22,508 --> 00:22:25,553
So I decided
to play it safe by purchasing items

430
00:22:25,636 --> 00:22:26,762
and face opponents aggressively.

431
00:22:26,846 --> 00:22:27,847
SANGHYUN TARGETS HORSEKING

432
00:22:27,930 --> 00:22:28,931
I'll discard the Shield.

433
00:22:29,014 --> 00:22:31,559
I'll discard one more.
I'll get rid of the Wrench.

434
00:22:32,601 --> 00:22:34,103
Give me two Pistols, please.

435
00:22:34,186 --> 00:22:35,896
BUY 2 CARDS WITH HIGHEST ATTACK STAT

436
00:22:35,980 --> 00:22:37,940
I made the strongest play I could.

437
00:22:38,023 --> 00:22:39,483
[dealer] Youn Sanghyun wins.

438
00:22:39,984 --> 00:22:40,985
Thank you.

439
00:22:50,077 --> 00:22:52,872
HORSEKING TAGGED ZZONE AND DDOLDDOL
SANGHYUN TAGGED HORSEKING

440
00:22:52,955 --> 00:22:55,165
[whispering] Horseking's just tagging
everyone like crazy.

441
00:22:55,249 --> 00:22:57,042
[panting]

442
00:23:04,383 --> 00:23:06,343
Give me one Wrench and one Shield, please.

443
00:23:06,427 --> 00:23:11,265
SHIELD 1, SHIELD 1, WRENCH 1

444
00:23:14,310 --> 00:23:19,523
I thought this could very likely
be my last game.

445
00:23:19,607 --> 00:23:23,736
This was the one game
where I could purely play on my own terms.

446
00:23:23,819 --> 00:23:26,614
I really wanted to go all-out
and play aggressively for once.

447
00:23:27,907 --> 00:23:31,327
There wasn't much time left,
but I decided to at least do something.

448
00:23:37,041 --> 00:23:39,585
[Sanghyun] Did you find something?
Are you going to tag me?

449
00:23:39,668 --> 00:23:40,878
I have a ton of coins.

450
00:23:46,008 --> 00:23:48,677
QUICKLY RETREATING TO THE STORE

451
00:23:49,678 --> 00:23:52,139
PARK JIMIN FAILS TO TAG YOUN SANGHYUN

452
00:23:52,222 --> 00:23:54,224
I couldn't tag Sanghyun.

453
00:23:55,100 --> 00:23:58,812
There was only one way
to the basement Store,

454
00:23:59,521 --> 00:24:02,316
so I waited at the entrance
for someone else to come by.

455
00:24:02,399 --> 00:24:04,693
[♪ tense music playing]

456
00:24:06,236 --> 00:24:08,656
JUST THEN, YUK JUNSEO COMES DOWNSTAIRS

457
00:24:10,699 --> 00:24:12,034
-Can I tag you?
-[Junseo] What?

458
00:24:12,826 --> 00:24:14,495
-Go ahead if you want.
-[Jimin] Really?

459
00:24:14,578 --> 00:24:17,915
Junseo said it so confidently,
but it felt like a bluff.

460
00:24:18,916 --> 00:24:20,376
PARK JIMIN TAGS YUK JUNSEO

461
00:24:20,459 --> 00:24:22,836
I figured, "Why not?"

462
00:24:22,920 --> 00:24:27,049
"When am I ever going to get a chance
to tag Yuk Junseo?" So I just went for it.

463
00:24:27,591 --> 00:24:31,053
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

464
00:24:31,136 --> 00:24:34,264
[dealer] Ms. Park Jimin,
please place your Attack card first.

465
00:24:41,397 --> 00:24:44,566
[Junseo] I had set myself up
with defense items then.

466
00:24:44,650 --> 00:24:47,152
I wasn't sure what would happen,
but for now...

467
00:24:51,991 --> 00:24:53,033
[dealer] Okay.

468
00:24:56,912 --> 00:24:59,957
JUNSEO'S CARD: MUTANT 4
JIMIN'S CARD: COMMANDER 5

469
00:25:00,040 --> 00:25:02,501
We will reveal the battle results.

470
00:25:05,379 --> 00:25:06,422
Here are the battle results.

471
00:25:09,049 --> 00:25:10,509
Yuk Junseo wins.

472
00:25:12,428 --> 00:25:14,763
-[Jimin] Ah...
-[♪ tense music playing]

473
00:25:14,847 --> 00:25:16,557
BARRICADE, MUTANT, SHIELD
WRENCH, COMMANDER

474
00:25:16,640 --> 00:25:18,809
JUNSEO'S CARDS
MUTANT 4, SHIELD 1, BARRICADE 3

475
00:25:18,892 --> 00:25:20,561
SHIELD ADDS 1 DEFENSE POINT
TOTAL 9 POINTS

476
00:25:20,644 --> 00:25:22,980
JIMIN'S CARDS
COMMANDER 5, WRENCH 1, TOTAL 6 POINTS

477
00:25:23,689 --> 00:25:26,942
JUNSEO DEFEATS JIMIN 9 TO 6

478
00:25:27,026 --> 00:25:29,820
[Junseo] I drew a Defense card,

479
00:25:29,903 --> 00:25:32,031
so I decided to play defensively.

480
00:25:32,823 --> 00:25:34,575
I'll just buy the Barricade.

481
00:25:34,658 --> 00:25:37,703
JUNSEO GOES ALL-IN ON DEFENSE

482
00:25:38,287 --> 00:25:41,790
I'm going to survive.
God hasn't abandoned me after all.

483
00:25:43,917 --> 00:25:46,003
[Jimin] I had really wanted
to beat Junseo.

484
00:25:46,712 --> 00:25:48,964
Whether I attack or defend,

485
00:25:49,048 --> 00:25:52,509
I realized that I needed to commit
to whatever I did.

486
00:25:52,593 --> 00:25:55,137
Still, I think that game with Junseo
was a huge help

487
00:25:55,220 --> 00:25:57,890
in figuring out my strategy going forward.

488
00:25:58,432 --> 00:26:01,518
I'm going to win with my brains.
I'm determined to make a comeback.

489
00:26:02,436 --> 00:26:04,563
[host] Round 1 is over.

490
00:26:04,646 --> 00:26:08,400
[♪ tense music playing]

491
00:26:08,484 --> 00:26:12,362
We will now announce
the top three players from Round 1.

492
00:26:13,572 --> 00:26:14,823
Horseking,

493
00:26:14,907 --> 00:26:17,034
Yuk Junseo,

494
00:26:17,117 --> 00:26:19,119
and Youn Sanghyun.

495
00:26:19,703 --> 00:26:21,622
TIED FOR 1ST
HORSEKING, JUNSEO, SANGHYUN

496
00:26:21,705 --> 00:26:23,832
2ND: JOONSU
TIED FOR 3RD: DDOLDDOL, JIMIN, ZZONE

497
00:26:23,916 --> 00:26:25,918
Did Sanghyun beat Horseking?

498
00:26:26,502 --> 00:26:27,503
Yes.

499
00:26:27,586 --> 00:26:28,796
Then, you have one point?

500
00:26:31,757 --> 00:26:34,718
There was a point difference
of only one or two.

501
00:26:34,802 --> 00:26:37,805
Why be in the top three
and become everyone else's target?

502
00:26:37,888 --> 00:26:40,057
I'd rather wait at the bottom
with minus one point

503
00:26:40,140 --> 00:26:42,643
and make a huge comeback
at the end to take first place.

504
00:26:43,227 --> 00:26:45,104
The scores are really close,

505
00:26:45,187 --> 00:26:48,107
so as long as I don't fall any further,
I still have a chance.

506
00:26:49,566 --> 00:26:51,735
But starting in Round 2,
we can lose our cards.

507
00:26:51,819 --> 00:26:53,946
Now, you lose a life with each loss.

508
00:26:56,782 --> 00:26:58,992
-[mic feedback]
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]

509
00:26:59,076 --> 00:27:02,204
[host] In a few moments,
the second and final round will begin.

510
00:27:02,287 --> 00:27:05,290
Round 2 will last 60 minutes.

511
00:27:05,791 --> 00:27:06,875
BEFORE THE START OF ROUND 1

512
00:27:06,959 --> 00:27:08,919
Round 2 will last for 60 minutes.

513
00:27:09,753 --> 00:27:12,089
And 20 minutes
after the start of the round,

514
00:27:12,172 --> 00:27:14,842
the chase area
and Store operations will change.

515
00:27:14,925 --> 00:27:15,926
Oh...

516
00:27:17,219 --> 00:27:21,974
After 20 minutes, the basement
and first floor will be excluded,

517
00:27:22,599 --> 00:27:26,436
and only the second and third floors
will remain part of the playable area.

518
00:27:26,520 --> 00:27:31,775
As a result, from that point onwards,
the basement Store will close.

519
00:27:32,734 --> 00:27:34,403
Ah...

520
00:27:34,987 --> 00:27:38,365
[alarm blaring]

521
00:27:38,448 --> 00:27:42,244
[host] Round 2 of "Dystopia"
will begin now.

522
00:27:44,162 --> 00:27:47,791
[♪ ominous music playing]

523
00:28:03,640 --> 00:28:05,058
Geez, that startled me.

524
00:28:07,853 --> 00:28:08,854
[ZZONE] Let's go.

525
00:28:09,354 --> 00:28:11,273
[host] Tag confirmed.

526
00:28:11,356 --> 00:28:15,152
-[Junseo] My target in Round 2 was ZZONE.
-[♪ exciting music playing]

527
00:28:15,736 --> 00:28:18,113
She was tagged in Round 1,

528
00:28:18,196 --> 00:28:21,783
and she probably couldn't find many coins,

529
00:28:21,867 --> 00:28:23,911
so I figured she didn't have
many cards either.

530
00:28:24,536 --> 00:28:26,413
[ZZONE] I knew for sure he'd do that.

531
00:28:26,955 --> 00:28:28,999
Since I didn't have many coins,

532
00:28:29,082 --> 00:28:33,170
I was thinking that I should quickly
find a bunch in Round 2.

533
00:28:33,670 --> 00:28:36,048
But I got tagged before I even could.

534
00:28:36,131 --> 00:28:37,925
So, I was like, "Fine, let's go."

535
00:28:38,842 --> 00:28:39,927
Hello.

536
00:28:40,010 --> 00:28:43,263
Since I'm already at minus one,
I had to go for points,

537
00:28:43,347 --> 00:28:45,557
and I might win if I'm lucky.

538
00:28:47,976 --> 00:28:52,689
Normally, when an Attacker
goes for a sure attack,

539
00:28:52,773 --> 00:28:53,982
they play the Commander card.

540
00:28:54,066 --> 00:28:58,070
But I thought then,
"What if she expects me to think that

541
00:28:58,153 --> 00:29:02,407
and plays the Slave card instead?"

542
00:29:02,491 --> 00:29:04,076
That was my thought process.

543
00:29:13,794 --> 00:29:15,128
JUNSEO SUBMITS SOLDIER CARD

544
00:29:15,212 --> 00:29:20,050
So I added Weapon Cards
to my Soldier card and attacked.

545
00:29:20,634 --> 00:29:22,177
JUNSEO'S CARDS
WRENCH 1, PISTOL 3

546
00:29:22,260 --> 00:29:23,804
ANTIDOTE, SOLDIER 3

547
00:29:23,887 --> 00:29:25,931
TOTAL 7 POINTS

548
00:29:26,598 --> 00:29:29,851
WHEN EQUIPPED WITH WRENCH,
ATTACK STAT GOES UP 1

549
00:29:29,935 --> 00:29:32,938
PISTOL AND WRENCH COMBINATION
RESULTS IN 1 EXTRA POINT

550
00:29:33,522 --> 00:29:36,316
JUNSEO'S FINAL ATTACK TOTAL
8 POINTS

551
00:29:39,861 --> 00:29:42,239
MUTANT, BULLETPROOF VEST, BULLETPROOF VEST

552
00:29:42,322 --> 00:29:44,408
ZZONE'S CARDS
MUTANT 4, BULLETPROOF VEST 2

553
00:29:44,491 --> 00:29:46,493
BULLETPROOF VEST 2
TOTAL 8 POINTS

554
00:29:47,077 --> 00:29:49,705
BOTH PLAYERS TIED AT 8 POINTS

555
00:29:50,914 --> 00:29:52,708
[dealer] ZZONE wins.

556
00:29:57,796 --> 00:30:00,090
Geez, why did you do that?

557
00:30:00,173 --> 00:30:02,259
DEFENSIVE EFFECT
OF ZZONE'S BULLETPROOF VEST CARD

558
00:30:02,342 --> 00:30:05,470
DEFENDER WINS IN THE EVENT OF A TIE

559
00:30:05,554 --> 00:30:07,514
-Ms. ZZONE, please take your cards...
-Gosh,

560
00:30:07,597 --> 00:30:10,559
I went all-in on defense,
and Sanghyun went all-in on attack.

561
00:30:11,768 --> 00:30:14,855
We were all basically going
into the same area.

562
00:30:14,938 --> 00:30:18,608
I thought that was when tags
would most likely occur.

563
00:30:18,692 --> 00:30:21,111
And I was sure I'd get tagged,
so I went to the Store.

564
00:30:21,695 --> 00:30:24,281
1 MINUTE BEFORE THE END OF ROUND 1

565
00:30:25,449 --> 00:30:30,245
[whispers] I'll buy this.
I'd like to buy the Bulletproof Vest.

566
00:30:30,871 --> 00:30:32,706
BOLDLY DISCARDS
BASIC SHIELD DEFENSE CARD

567
00:30:32,789 --> 00:30:34,583
I have to discard the card.

568
00:30:35,751 --> 00:30:39,671
SWAPS FOR BULLETPROOF VEST CARD
WITH GOOD EFFECT

569
00:30:39,755 --> 00:30:41,631
SHIELD 1, SHIELD 1, SHIELD 1

570
00:30:41,715 --> 00:30:44,259
[ZZONE]
Yeah, I think that helped me a lot.

571
00:30:44,342 --> 00:30:46,678
I was finally starting
to earn points little by little,

572
00:30:46,762 --> 00:30:48,263
so I felt great.

573
00:30:50,932 --> 00:30:53,435
[♪ tense music playing]

574
00:30:53,518 --> 00:30:56,396
[Junseo] I screwed up.
It hurt my pride a little.

575
00:30:56,480 --> 00:30:58,899
I just made the wrong call.

576
00:31:00,859 --> 00:31:01,943
-[dealer] Mr. Yuk Junseo.
-Yes?

577
00:31:02,027 --> 00:31:05,280
Since you used an Antidote card,
your Character Card is not eliminated.

578
00:31:05,363 --> 00:31:06,364
Okay.

579
00:31:08,533 --> 00:31:09,785
[sighs in frustration]

580
00:31:11,453 --> 00:31:14,289
What a fucking idiot.

581
00:31:15,791 --> 00:31:17,918
I lost everything
except my Character Card.

582
00:31:18,710 --> 00:31:20,921
I'd used up all my items too

583
00:31:22,047 --> 00:31:23,757
and barely had any money left.

584
00:31:23,840 --> 00:31:25,717
I didn't have many coins at that point.

585
00:31:28,261 --> 00:31:30,847
So I went back
to looking for coins like crazy.

586
00:31:30,931 --> 00:31:34,142
That's how I could buy cards again
and recover.

587
00:31:34,810 --> 00:31:36,853
I went everywhere, searching every corner,

588
00:31:38,188 --> 00:31:41,233
and I actually started
finding them little by little.

589
00:31:41,817 --> 00:31:43,652
I'd find two coins here, one coin there,

590
00:31:43,735 --> 00:31:47,447
or even three coins in a row
stuck in lockers.

591
00:31:48,740 --> 00:31:50,367
And while I was searching...

592
00:31:54,913 --> 00:31:56,706
I found a silver box.

593
00:31:56,790 --> 00:31:58,959
I opened it,
and there were 10 coins inside.

594
00:32:00,293 --> 00:32:04,714
So I started thinking again,
"Maybe I still have hope."

595
00:32:04,798 --> 00:32:07,008
I felt I still had
plenty of time to recover.

596
00:32:10,929 --> 00:32:12,347
[Horseking] After 20 minutes,

597
00:32:12,430 --> 00:32:14,182
I figured everyone
would start focusing on attacking.

598
00:32:14,266 --> 00:32:16,852
So, I decided
I wasn't going to attack anymore.

599
00:32:16,935 --> 00:32:18,019
I'll only focus on defense.

600
00:32:21,314 --> 00:32:23,150
[exhales sharply] Let's make a deal.

601
00:32:26,278 --> 00:32:28,905
If the others keep fighting each other
into the negatives,

602
00:32:29,489 --> 00:32:31,116
I can win if I just maintain my score.

603
00:32:34,828 --> 00:32:36,121
Well, in that case...

604
00:32:39,541 --> 00:32:42,252
I'll sell my Citizen, Soldier,
and Commander cards.

605
00:32:42,878 --> 00:32:44,462
I'll sell these three cards.

606
00:32:44,546 --> 00:32:48,383
[dealer] Mr. Horseking, you have sold
your Citizen, Soldier, and Commander cards

607
00:32:48,466 --> 00:32:50,177
and acquired 30 coins.

608
00:32:50,260 --> 00:32:52,554
[Horseking]
As I'll be focusing entirely on defense,

609
00:32:52,637 --> 00:32:56,141
I won't need my attack cards anymore,
so I'll sell them.

610
00:32:56,892 --> 00:32:58,435
I'll take one Smoke Bomb.

611
00:32:59,060 --> 00:33:00,520
SMOKE BOMB
NULLIFIES CURRENT BATTLE

612
00:33:00,604 --> 00:33:03,440
WORTH 15 COINS
SPECIAL WEAPON CARD THAT NULLIFIES BATTLE

613
00:33:04,191 --> 00:33:06,067
I'll buy one more of these.

614
00:33:06,151 --> 00:33:09,070
TAKES THE 30 COINS HE ACQUIRED
AND SPENDS THEM ON 2 SMOKE BOMBS

615
00:33:09,654 --> 00:33:11,114
[Horseking]
If I focused solely on defense,

616
00:33:11,198 --> 00:33:12,449
there was no way I'd lose.

617
00:33:12,532 --> 00:33:17,537
The Smoke Bomb can nullify
whatever card my opponent plays,

618
00:33:17,621 --> 00:33:20,415
so as long as I kept
Smoke Bombs on me with a high score,

619
00:33:20,498 --> 00:33:22,375
I thought there was no way I could lose.

620
00:33:22,459 --> 00:33:25,795
ROUND 1 RESULTS
JIMIN AT THE BOTTOM WITH NEGATIVE 1 POINT

621
00:33:27,172 --> 00:33:29,049
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

622
00:33:30,634 --> 00:33:31,718
Hello.

623
00:33:32,344 --> 00:33:35,805
I realized I really needed
to rack up a lot of points,

624
00:33:35,889 --> 00:33:38,350
so I decided to play
really aggressively in Round 2.

625
00:33:38,433 --> 00:33:40,727
That means I'd need to buy a lot of cards,

626
00:33:40,810 --> 00:33:43,063
but I can only hold three cards.

627
00:33:43,146 --> 00:33:44,898
So, how do I solve that?

628
00:33:45,982 --> 00:33:48,151
SPECIAL WEAPONS

629
00:33:50,070 --> 00:33:51,154
The Secret Vault.

630
00:33:51,238 --> 00:33:52,530
ALLOWS YOU TO HOLD FOUR CARDS

631
00:33:52,614 --> 00:33:54,366
BUYS SECRET VAULT
SPECIAL WEAPON CARD

632
00:33:54,449 --> 00:33:55,450
15 COINS

633
00:33:55,533 --> 00:33:58,119
[Jimin] It was really expensive,
so I hesitated.

634
00:33:58,203 --> 00:34:01,748
But if I bought a Secret Vault,
I could hold up to four cards.

635
00:34:01,831 --> 00:34:05,710
I was determined to do whatever it takes
to beat everyone this round,

636
00:34:05,794 --> 00:34:06,795
so I bought it.

637
00:34:07,379 --> 00:34:08,421
SHIELD 1, SHIELD 1

638
00:34:08,505 --> 00:34:11,925
JIMIN'S CARD SLOTS INCREASE

639
00:34:15,762 --> 00:34:18,515
Secret... First, I'll buy a Pistol.

640
00:34:19,808 --> 00:34:20,892
And I'll buy a Knife.

641
00:34:20,976 --> 00:34:22,727
KNIFE
LOOT 1 EXTRA COIN IN EVENT OF WIN

642
00:34:22,811 --> 00:34:25,855
SHIELD, SHIELD, PISTOL, KNIFE

643
00:34:25,939 --> 00:34:28,358
[Jimin] I stocked up on Attack cards.

644
00:34:28,441 --> 00:34:30,527
I really wanted to tag someone.

645
00:34:30,610 --> 00:34:32,279
Let me get in on the tagging too.

646
00:34:36,700 --> 00:34:38,201
I need to tag. Where is everyone?

647
00:34:38,285 --> 00:34:39,452
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

648
00:34:43,790 --> 00:34:46,418
MEANWHILE, LEE JOONSU IS LOOKING FOR COINS

649
00:34:48,003 --> 00:34:49,796
You find coins so well. Where were they?

650
00:34:49,879 --> 00:34:51,339
-Where were they?
-I didn't find them.

651
00:34:51,423 --> 00:34:52,757
Then, where did you get them?

652
00:34:53,383 --> 00:34:55,176
-[host] Tag confirmed.
-Tag.

653
00:34:55,260 --> 00:34:56,261
JIMIN TAGS JOONSU

654
00:34:56,344 --> 00:34:58,847
-[♪ exciting music playing]
-Right then, Joonsu happened to walk by.

655
00:34:58,930 --> 00:35:02,934
If you want to tag me, go ahead.
But I'm still going to win.

656
00:35:03,560 --> 00:35:06,104
I had a lot of coins,
so I bought a lot of items.

657
00:35:06,187 --> 00:35:07,981
I went all-in on defense,

658
00:35:08,064 --> 00:35:09,733
so I had nothing to be afraid of.

659
00:35:13,028 --> 00:35:16,865
[dealer] Ms. Park Jimin,
please submit your card face down.

660
00:35:17,490 --> 00:35:20,619
[Jimin] I really want to fight and win,
no matter what.

661
00:35:24,372 --> 00:35:27,959
If you want to attack, go for it.
I'm going to do my best to defend.

662
00:35:33,673 --> 00:35:36,635
[Jimin] I thought over
which Character Card to play.

663
00:35:36,718 --> 00:35:37,802
COMMANDER, SOLDIER, SLAVE

664
00:35:37,886 --> 00:35:40,847
I needed the highest possible attack power
from my Character Card.

665
00:35:40,930 --> 00:35:43,600
The highest attack stat is five points,

666
00:35:43,683 --> 00:35:46,519
while the highest defense stat
is only four points.

667
00:35:46,603 --> 00:35:50,023
So of course, playing the Commander
would be the best choice.

668
00:35:50,106 --> 00:35:52,692
But if the Slave and Commander
go up against each other,

669
00:35:52,776 --> 00:35:55,320
the Commander would become
completely useless.

670
00:35:55,403 --> 00:35:56,488
Here you go.

671
00:35:59,699 --> 00:36:01,993
So, after some deliberation,
I played my card.

672
00:36:04,120 --> 00:36:05,664
[Joonsu] I had nothing to be afraid of.

673
00:36:08,333 --> 00:36:10,585
[dealer] We will check the battle results.

674
00:36:11,127 --> 00:36:12,796
SHIELD, BARRICADE
KNIFE, PISTOL

675
00:36:12,879 --> 00:36:15,340
CARD POINTS FOR BOTH PLAYERS,
EXCLUDING CHARACTER CARDS

676
00:36:16,091 --> 00:36:18,927
4 POINTS, 1 EXTRA POINT

677
00:36:19,010 --> 00:36:20,553
TOTAL 5 DEFENSE POINTS

678
00:36:20,637 --> 00:36:23,139
TOTAL 5 ATTACK POINTS

679
00:36:23,640 --> 00:36:26,434
IF WEAPON CARDS TIE,
BATTLE DETERMINED BY CHARACTER CARD POINTS

680
00:36:30,480 --> 00:36:34,359
I thought there was no way I could lose
with nine points of defense.

681
00:36:34,984 --> 00:36:36,444
MUTANT, SHIELD, BARRICADE

682
00:36:36,528 --> 00:36:39,447
LEE JOONSU SUBMITTED THE MUTANT
INSTEAD OF THE SLAVE

683
00:36:39,531 --> 00:36:40,532
[♪ exciting music playing]

684
00:36:40,615 --> 00:36:43,868
[Joonsu] With the Barricade combination,
I get an extra point to make it 9,

685
00:36:43,952 --> 00:36:46,121
and that's a pretty high point total.

686
00:36:46,996 --> 00:36:48,748
HORSEKING AND ZZONE TIED AT 5

687
00:36:48,832 --> 00:36:50,583
HORSEKING DEFEATED DDOLDDOL 5 TO 4

688
00:36:50,667 --> 00:36:52,377
SANGHYUN AND HORSEKING TIED AT 9

689
00:36:52,460 --> 00:36:54,295
JUNSEO DEFEATED JIMIN 9 TO 6

690
00:36:54,379 --> 00:36:56,297
JUNSEO AND ZZONE TIED AT 8

691
00:36:56,881 --> 00:36:59,718
JOONSU COMBINED CARDS FOR 9 POINTS,
HIGHEST BATTLE SCORE SO FAR

692
00:37:01,970 --> 00:37:03,430
[dealer] Park Jimin wins.

693
00:37:07,350 --> 00:37:12,105
Considering what had happened
and how things had progressed so far,

694
00:37:12,689 --> 00:37:16,359
it was obvious that Joonsu
was very confident in his defense,

695
00:37:16,443 --> 00:37:19,487
so I figured there was no way
he'd play the Slave right now.

696
00:37:20,238 --> 00:37:21,573
KNIFE, PISTOL, COMMANDER

697
00:37:21,656 --> 00:37:23,283
-I decided to play the Commander.
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]

698
00:37:28,997 --> 00:37:30,623
Finally, I won.

699
00:37:31,666 --> 00:37:35,295
Thanks to the Secret Vault,
I was able to hold more cards,

700
00:37:35,378 --> 00:37:36,755
and I think that helped me win.

701
00:37:38,047 --> 00:37:41,092
[dealer] Since you lost the battle,
your Character Card is eliminated.

702
00:37:41,176 --> 00:37:43,428
JOONSU'S MUTANT IS ELIMINATED

703
00:37:46,097 --> 00:37:49,559
[Joonsu] I was devastated since it felt
like my whole strategy was all wrong.

704
00:37:49,642 --> 00:37:52,562
I felt flustered, frustrated,
and really annoyed.

705
00:37:56,191 --> 00:37:59,110
[host] Beginning now,
Round 2's chase area will be changed.

706
00:38:01,488 --> 00:38:02,655
[Joonsu] Did you find any coins?

707
00:38:02,739 --> 00:38:05,742
Yeah, I found some,
but I don't think there are any more,

708
00:38:05,825 --> 00:38:07,577
so I'm going to the Store.

709
00:38:08,495 --> 00:38:10,955
The Store...
There's one on the second floor.

710
00:38:14,542 --> 00:38:16,294
[ZZONE] Is everyone going to the Store?

711
00:38:17,587 --> 00:38:18,880
[Ddolddol] Do you still have
a lot of coins?

712
00:38:18,963 --> 00:38:20,006
LONG LINE OUTSIDE THE STORE

713
00:38:21,216 --> 00:38:22,550
Hello.

714
00:38:23,134 --> 00:38:26,471
Since the point differential
wasn't really that dramatic...

715
00:38:26,554 --> 00:38:27,555
1ST HORSEKING, SANGHYUN

716
00:38:27,639 --> 00:38:29,641
2ND JUNSEO, ZZONE, JIMIN
3RD JOONSU, DDOLDDOL

717
00:38:29,724 --> 00:38:32,435
I didn't necessarily
have to play defensively,

718
00:38:32,519 --> 00:38:33,853
and I could go on the attack too.

719
00:38:34,646 --> 00:38:37,273
I decided to stock up on items first.

720
00:38:38,608 --> 00:38:42,695
ZZONE PURCHASES A TRAP AND A BUNKER

721
00:38:43,238 --> 00:38:46,741
PLAYERS TAKE TURNS BUYING CARDS

722
00:38:52,872 --> 00:38:54,457
[whispers] A Grenade...

723
00:38:55,083 --> 00:38:56,167
I'll buy an Antidote.

724
00:38:56,251 --> 00:38:57,919
JOONSU BUYS A GRENADE AND ANTIDOTE

725
00:39:00,046 --> 00:39:02,549
Joonsu's pockets
are looking a lot lighter now.

726
00:39:02,632 --> 00:39:04,592
-[Joonsu] They sure are.
-[♪ serious music playing]

727
00:39:05,510 --> 00:39:08,847
JOONSU RETURNS

728
00:39:11,182 --> 00:39:12,433
GLANCES

729
00:39:15,854 --> 00:39:17,605
Ah, what do I do?

730
00:39:24,863 --> 00:39:26,823
-Let's go.
-[host] Tag confirmed.

731
00:39:27,365 --> 00:39:28,575
My only target was Jimin.

732
00:39:28,658 --> 00:39:31,953
Once I fixate on something,
I zero in on only that thing.

733
00:39:32,036 --> 00:39:35,874
Since she came after me first,
I was only going to go after her.

734
00:39:36,708 --> 00:39:38,334
Hey, I was in line waiting!

735
00:39:38,877 --> 00:39:40,378
Oh, yeah!

736
00:39:42,255 --> 00:39:45,300
[Jimin] Joonsu was so cheap.

737
00:39:46,217 --> 00:39:50,096
It's an unwritten rule.
It's about basic manners.

738
00:39:50,179 --> 00:39:54,517
If someone's waiting in line at the Store,
you let them buy first before the battle.

739
00:39:54,601 --> 00:39:57,937
But he bought everything he wanted
and tagged me as soon as he came out.

740
00:39:58,021 --> 00:39:59,689
I got so mad.

741
00:40:03,318 --> 00:40:04,319
[Junseo] Where did everyone go?

742
00:40:04,402 --> 00:40:05,862
Joonsu tagged Jimin.

743
00:40:05,945 --> 00:40:06,946
[Sanghyun] For real?

744
00:40:07,030 --> 00:40:08,948
He really did. Check your phone.

745
00:40:09,032 --> 00:40:10,158
Check your phone.

746
00:40:10,241 --> 00:40:13,119
-[Sanghyun] But that's so brutal.
-[ZZONE] Yeah.

747
00:40:13,202 --> 00:40:15,288
That's so brutal to do
in front of the Store.

748
00:40:15,371 --> 00:40:17,624
That's the kind of play
only Joonsu could pull off.

749
00:40:18,875 --> 00:40:21,502
[dealer] Mr. Lee Joonsu,
please submit your card first.

750
00:40:22,128 --> 00:40:24,339
[Joonsu humming]

751
00:40:25,632 --> 00:40:28,009
[Joonsu] I'm just going to go all in now.

752
00:40:28,843 --> 00:40:31,304
JOONSU SUBMITS HIS CARD

753
00:40:32,889 --> 00:40:35,725
I didn't have any cards left at the time.

754
00:40:36,768 --> 00:40:38,019
Just a moment, please.

755
00:40:38,102 --> 00:40:40,021
JIMIN GOT TAGGED
WHILE IN LINE FOR THE STORE

756
00:40:40,104 --> 00:40:41,189
[Jimin] Geez, my coins...

757
00:40:42,523 --> 00:40:46,486
As I was trying to figure out
what to do...

758
00:40:48,696 --> 00:40:50,740
[dealer] Okay, both players
have submitted their cards.

759
00:40:51,407 --> 00:40:54,494
JIMIN SUBMITS HER CARD

760
00:40:55,078 --> 00:40:56,829
I want to know how their battle turns out.

761
00:40:56,913 --> 00:40:58,039
-[♪ curious music playing]
-Me too.

762
00:40:58,122 --> 00:41:00,041
-I'm curious.
-I can't wait to find out.

763
00:41:01,084 --> 00:41:03,086
[Jimin] Hey, let me go to the Store first!

764
00:41:03,169 --> 00:41:04,170
[Joonsu] Let's go.

765
00:41:05,505 --> 00:41:06,631
[Ddolddol] So, what happened with you two?

766
00:41:07,924 --> 00:41:09,968
[Joonsu] It's insane. She won.

767
00:41:10,051 --> 00:41:12,011
-[Ddolddol] How did you win?
-[ZZONE] It was unbelievable.

768
00:41:12,095 --> 00:41:13,680
-[Jimin laughs cutely]
-[Ddolddol] How did you beat him?

769
00:41:14,555 --> 00:41:17,392
[Joonsu humming]

770
00:41:17,475 --> 00:41:21,104
I was angry because it felt like
he was gloating, but then...

771
00:41:22,146 --> 00:41:23,356
I looked and realized

772
00:41:23,439 --> 00:41:26,943
he put together
everything he had to attack me.

773
00:41:27,694 --> 00:41:30,697
So, that meant he'd definitely play
the Commander card,

774
00:41:30,780 --> 00:41:33,658
and he'd try to make his attack
the highest point total possible.

775
00:41:34,242 --> 00:41:36,619
JOONSU'S SCORE
COMMANDER 5, ANTIDOTE, GRENADE 5

776
00:41:36,703 --> 00:41:37,704
TOTAL 10 POINTS

777
00:41:37,787 --> 00:41:41,332
There was no way
I could beat him with the cards I had,

778
00:41:42,375 --> 00:41:43,876
so I decided to play the Slave card.

779
00:41:45,086 --> 00:41:47,213
When the Slave goes up
against the Commander,

780
00:41:47,296 --> 00:41:49,882
the Commander becomes completely useless.

781
00:41:51,092 --> 00:41:53,177
[dealer] Park Jimin wins.

782
00:41:53,261 --> 00:41:54,345
What was that, Jimin?

783
00:41:55,680 --> 00:41:56,681
Gosh, okay.

784
00:41:56,764 --> 00:41:58,182
ACCURATE READ EARNS JIMIN 1 POINT

785
00:41:58,266 --> 00:42:02,020
I think as long as you have
the guts and the nerve,

786
00:42:02,103 --> 00:42:05,314
the Slave is all you need to win.

787
00:42:07,066 --> 00:42:08,401
How did you win?

788
00:42:08,484 --> 00:42:10,486
[in English] Fuck! [yells]

789
00:42:10,987 --> 00:42:12,613
[in Korean] I was so mad.

790
00:42:12,697 --> 00:42:15,575
My cards were pretty strong,
but Jimin kept winning.

791
00:42:16,325 --> 00:42:17,785
LOST FIRST MATCH 10 TO 9

792
00:42:18,286 --> 00:42:20,747
HIS COMMANDER LOST TO HER SLAVE
IN SECOND MATCH

793
00:42:20,830 --> 00:42:23,624
I kept losing to Jimin.
I don't understand why I keep losing.

794
00:42:23,708 --> 00:42:25,251
LOST TWICE IN A ROW DESPITE HIGH SCORES

795
00:42:26,419 --> 00:42:29,130
[sighs] How am I supposed to attack?

796
00:42:33,926 --> 00:42:34,927
Whatever. Fuck it.

797
00:42:35,011 --> 00:42:36,888
[♪ serious music playing]

798
00:42:36,971 --> 00:42:40,224
I kept losing, and that made me
want to win even more.

799
00:42:40,308 --> 00:42:41,851
JOONSU APPROACHES JIMIN AS SHE WAITS

800
00:42:41,934 --> 00:42:43,352
-Are you going to buy something?
-No.

801
00:42:43,436 --> 00:42:45,646
-Are you here to tag again?
-Yes, to tag someone.

802
00:42:45,730 --> 00:42:47,648
Listen, I really need to buy stuff.

803
00:42:47,732 --> 00:42:49,650
[Joonsu laughs]

804
00:42:49,734 --> 00:42:52,070
I couldn't buy anything
because of you earlier.

805
00:42:52,653 --> 00:42:54,655
What's the strongest one right now?

806
00:42:55,573 --> 00:42:57,325
The next strongest one
after the Commander...

807
00:42:57,992 --> 00:43:01,245
[Jimin] But he kept getting on my nerves,

808
00:43:01,329 --> 00:43:04,165
and I couldn't hide it on my face.

809
00:43:07,251 --> 00:43:09,712
[Joonsu] I actually still had
my Commander card.

810
00:43:10,213 --> 00:43:14,509
I used an Antidote in the last battle,
so I didn't lose my Commander.

811
00:43:14,592 --> 00:43:16,719
[♪ exciting music playing]

812
00:43:16,803 --> 00:43:19,931
Jimin doesn't know
I still have my Commander card,

813
00:43:20,014 --> 00:43:22,225
so I decided to
attack her again one last time.

814
00:43:24,769 --> 00:43:25,853
Whatever!

815
00:43:26,646 --> 00:43:28,064
No, seriously. Come on.

816
00:43:28,147 --> 00:43:30,066
-Let's go.
-No, I'm serious.

817
00:43:30,149 --> 00:43:31,901
-[Joonsu] Let's go.
-No, hold on.

818
00:43:31,984 --> 00:43:33,319
[host] Tag confirmed.

819
00:43:33,903 --> 00:43:36,948
-Why are you coming after me, you punk?
-I don't know.

820
00:43:38,699 --> 00:43:39,784
You tagged her again?

821
00:43:40,701 --> 00:43:43,371
[Jimin] He won't even let me buy anything!

822
00:43:43,454 --> 00:43:44,455
[Horseking] You still haven't bought
anything yet?

823
00:43:44,539 --> 00:43:45,998
Oh, you couldn't.

824
00:43:49,961 --> 00:43:53,965
I was pretty much tied
with Horseking and Sanghyun though.

825
00:43:55,174 --> 00:43:58,010
But if she couldn't even get
in the Store, then Jimin...

826
00:43:58,094 --> 00:43:59,971
[Sanghyun] He just wants
to keep battling her.

827
00:44:00,054 --> 00:44:01,055
That puts her at a disadvantage.

828
00:44:01,139 --> 00:44:02,390
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

829
00:44:06,727 --> 00:44:08,980
[dealer] Mr. Lee Joonsu,
please submit your card.

830
00:44:09,063 --> 00:44:10,064
Okay.

831
00:44:11,482 --> 00:44:13,776
JOONSU SUBMITS HIS COMMANDER CARD

832
00:44:14,485 --> 00:44:17,280
[Jimin] I didn't have
any Weapon Cards at all.

833
00:44:17,363 --> 00:44:21,450
If he's attacking me that confidently,
it means he must have something.

834
00:44:25,079 --> 00:44:27,498
I said, "Screw it. Whatever."
And I played my card.

835
00:44:29,375 --> 00:44:32,378
ONE CARD SUBMITTED BY EACH PLAYER

836
00:44:33,629 --> 00:44:35,590
Damn it, Joonsu.

837
00:44:36,507 --> 00:44:38,134
[Joonsu] I can't lose more than twice.

838
00:44:38,718 --> 00:44:40,178
[Joonsu sighs]

839
00:44:41,137 --> 00:44:43,097
-[dealer] We will announce the results.
-[Joonsu] Okay.

840
00:44:43,181 --> 00:44:44,640
[dealer] The winner is...

841
00:44:47,518 --> 00:44:49,353
-Park Jimin.
-Okay.

842
00:44:49,437 --> 00:44:51,063
WINNER: PARK JIMIN
LOSER: LEE JOONSU

843
00:44:51,147 --> 00:44:52,356
COMMANDER, SLAVE

844
00:44:52,440 --> 00:44:54,734
[Jimin]
I thought he might've still had that card.

845
00:44:54,817 --> 00:44:55,860
JIMIN PLAYS SLAVE CARD AGAIN

846
00:44:56,819 --> 00:44:58,946
Try tagging me again and I'll kill you.

847
00:44:59,030 --> 00:45:01,866
I thought I needed to be strong to win,

848
00:45:01,949 --> 00:45:04,035
but after beating Joonsu twice,

849
00:45:04,785 --> 00:45:07,371
I really like using the Slave card.

850
00:45:08,247 --> 00:45:10,541
1ST PARK JIMIN, 2 POINTS

851
00:45:11,250 --> 00:45:12,752
[Horseking] She suddenly has two points.

852
00:45:12,835 --> 00:45:15,630
Jimin? I know. Now, we should be nervous.

853
00:45:17,548 --> 00:45:19,675
PARK JIMIN
RANKING: 1, SCORE: 2

854
00:45:20,176 --> 00:45:21,344
[Jimin] I should just hide.

855
00:45:22,345 --> 00:45:25,473
If I lose any more points here,

856
00:45:25,556 --> 00:45:27,516
I might not be able to advance.

857
00:45:27,600 --> 00:45:31,354
So I decided to watch
how everyone else's battles played out

858
00:45:31,437 --> 00:45:32,563
before making a move.

859
00:45:32,647 --> 00:45:36,234
And I kept looking here and there
for places to hide.

860
00:45:47,203 --> 00:45:48,287
[sighs in frustration]

861
00:45:48,913 --> 00:45:49,997
[Joonsu] I'm screwed.

862
00:45:57,171 --> 00:45:58,214
[grunts]

863
00:45:58,297 --> 00:45:59,799
[♪ moody music playing]

864
00:46:09,600 --> 00:46:11,727
Getting tagged by Jimin at first

865
00:46:11,811 --> 00:46:13,479
started all this, and because of that...

866
00:46:13,562 --> 00:46:15,231
[dealer] Park Jimin wins.

867
00:46:15,856 --> 00:46:17,149
-[Joonsu] I went into the negatives.
-[in English] Fuck!

868
00:46:17,233 --> 00:46:18,651
[in Korean] I lost my mind and went crazy.

869
00:46:18,734 --> 00:46:21,320
It's so frustrating and annoying.

870
00:46:23,489 --> 00:46:24,740
[sighs heavily]

871
00:46:28,828 --> 00:46:31,330
JUNSEO TAGGED ZZONE
JIMIN TAGGED JOONSU

872
00:46:31,414 --> 00:46:33,874
JOONSU TAGGED JIMIN
JOONSU TAGGED JIMIN

873
00:46:35,209 --> 00:46:37,420
[Ddolddol] There's a lot of tagging
happening right now,

874
00:46:37,503 --> 00:46:40,756
so I thought, "This isn't going to work.
I need to go on the offensive."

875
00:46:40,840 --> 00:46:43,801
Who knows when someone might tag me
or I might tag anyone?

876
00:46:43,884 --> 00:46:48,139
So first, I decided to max out
the item cards I had equipped.

877
00:46:48,222 --> 00:46:51,434
I'll buy these two. Radiation and Grenade.

878
00:46:52,518 --> 00:46:55,354
The Grenade adds
five points in attack stat.

879
00:46:55,438 --> 00:47:00,693
I also bought Radiation, which nullifies
the effects of my opponent's Weapon Cards.

880
00:47:00,776 --> 00:47:02,945
I equipped myself with all the best cards.

881
00:47:03,029 --> 00:47:06,407
I was going all-in on attack
to take everyone out.

882
00:47:07,158 --> 00:47:08,617
[Sanghyun] Did you find someone to tag?

883
00:47:09,160 --> 00:47:10,161
[Ddolddol] Who should I go for?

884
00:47:10,661 --> 00:47:12,705
ZZONE might be an easy target.

885
00:47:12,788 --> 00:47:13,789
Is she hiding?

886
00:47:13,873 --> 00:47:15,249
[Sanghyun] Yeah, she's likely hiding.

887
00:47:15,333 --> 00:47:16,625
[Ddolddol] Okay, good.

888
00:47:17,752 --> 00:47:19,545
Tag! Tag!

889
00:47:19,628 --> 00:47:21,047
AFTER ZZONE WAS TAGGED IN "KINGMAKER"

890
00:47:21,797 --> 00:47:23,924
[dealer] ZZONE has won.

891
00:47:24,008 --> 00:47:26,427
KIM DDOLDDOL LOST TO HER

892
00:47:27,136 --> 00:47:28,137
[ZZONE] It's over!

893
00:47:29,138 --> 00:47:31,724
[Ddolddol] I've had a bit of a grudge
since "Kingmaker."

894
00:47:32,308 --> 00:47:34,226
I immediately set out to find ZZONE.

895
00:47:34,810 --> 00:47:35,811
[Ddolddol] Have you seen ZZONE?

896
00:47:35,895 --> 00:47:36,979
I haven't.

897
00:47:37,605 --> 00:47:38,606
[Joonsu] Where are you going?

898
00:47:38,689 --> 00:47:39,774
[Ddolddol] I'm on my way to tag ZZONE.

899
00:47:40,649 --> 00:47:42,276
I set out to find that pink hair.

900
00:47:42,818 --> 00:47:44,487
ZZONE, where did this woman go?

901
00:47:45,988 --> 00:47:48,074
She's so hard to find.

902
00:47:49,867 --> 00:47:52,036
[ZZONE] I didn't have many coins,

903
00:47:52,119 --> 00:47:53,954
so I kept thinking,
"I need to find coins."

904
00:47:56,165 --> 00:47:59,043
-[Ddolddol] ZZONE! [laughs]
-[ZZONE] What? [groans]

905
00:48:00,378 --> 00:48:01,962
-[Ddolddol] Come on, let's battle.
-[ZZONE] No, don't.

906
00:48:02,046 --> 00:48:03,923
-[Ddolddol] Just once.
-[ZZONE] No, thanks.

907
00:48:04,006 --> 00:48:07,635
-ZZONE! If I catch you, you're dead!
-[ZZONE] No!

908
00:48:08,344 --> 00:48:10,179
-ZZONE.
-Please, no.

909
00:48:10,262 --> 00:48:11,847
DDOLDDOL TAGS ZZONE

910
00:48:11,931 --> 00:48:13,391
[host] Tag confirmed.

911
00:48:13,474 --> 00:48:14,850
I got that girl.

912
00:48:14,934 --> 00:48:18,062
She resisted, but it didn't work.

913
00:48:18,145 --> 00:48:20,439
I wanted to take ZZONE out.

914
00:48:22,316 --> 00:48:23,359
I needed coins...

915
00:48:24,318 --> 00:48:25,528
[groans]

916
00:48:25,611 --> 00:48:26,904
Geez.

917
00:48:26,987 --> 00:48:29,323
-This is so frustrating.
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]

918
00:48:30,491 --> 00:48:32,076
[Ddolddol]
I hope you have a good card, ZZONE.

919
00:48:32,785 --> 00:48:33,786
I felt bad,

920
00:48:33,869 --> 00:48:35,538
but I'm sorry, I'm not sorry.

921
00:48:35,621 --> 00:48:38,916
What can you do? It's a survival game.
I have to look out for myself.

922
00:48:40,709 --> 00:48:43,546
[dealer] Mr. Ddolddol
has submitted his cards.

923
00:48:50,136 --> 00:48:52,346
-Okay.
-Why did you submit so many cards?

924
00:48:54,014 --> 00:48:55,641
[dealer] We will check who the winner is.

925
00:48:59,270 --> 00:49:01,605
[ZZONE] I did have some cards though.

926
00:49:02,314 --> 00:49:05,693
[Ddolddol] I went in
knowing I was going to win,

927
00:49:05,776 --> 00:49:07,153
so I was 100% sure I had won.

928
00:49:08,320 --> 00:49:09,738
[dealer] We will reveal the results.

929
00:49:15,119 --> 00:49:16,370
ZZONE wins.

930
00:49:16,912 --> 00:49:18,038
[♪ tense music playing]

931
00:49:18,706 --> 00:49:20,166
[ZZONE] That felt so thrilling.

932
00:49:21,292 --> 00:49:22,751
[Ddolddol] I was completely shocked.

933
00:49:23,878 --> 00:49:26,672
I just dumped 22 coins into this battle.

934
00:49:26,755 --> 00:49:29,300
Why did I lose?
What's with this girl? What did she play?

935
00:49:29,383 --> 00:49:31,635
I was dying to know.

936
00:49:32,428 --> 00:49:35,014
SOLDIER, GRENADE, RADIATION
BUNKER, TRAP, MUTANT

937
00:49:36,474 --> 00:49:38,642
[host] The Radiation card played
by Kim Ddolddol

938
00:49:38,726 --> 00:49:40,686
and the Trap card played by ZZONE

939
00:49:40,769 --> 00:49:45,774
both nullify the attack and defense
of the opponent's most expensive weapon.

940
00:49:45,858 --> 00:49:49,320
As a result, Kim Ddolddol's Grenade

941
00:49:49,403 --> 00:49:52,198
and ZZONE's Bunker were both eliminated.

942
00:49:52,281 --> 00:49:54,658
After calculating the points
of the remaining cards,

943
00:49:54,742 --> 00:49:59,038
with Kim Ddolddol's four points
and ZZONE's five points,

944
00:49:59,121 --> 00:50:00,915
ZZONE wins.

945
00:50:01,790 --> 00:50:04,543
It was hilarious,
because I wanted to get tagged

946
00:50:04,627 --> 00:50:06,086
and I didn't have any points.

947
00:50:06,170 --> 00:50:07,796
But if I seem confident...

948
00:50:07,880 --> 00:50:10,549
They might play it safe
if you seem too confident.

949
00:50:11,091 --> 00:50:13,969
So I decided to bluff a little.

950
00:50:14,053 --> 00:50:15,804
I was trying so hard not to laugh.

951
00:50:15,888 --> 00:50:19,892
From the start, I thought there was no way
I could lose with that much defense.

952
00:50:21,185 --> 00:50:22,728
ZZONE, you're pretty smart.

953
00:50:22,811 --> 00:50:24,313
Why did you have to go and tag me?

954
00:50:27,733 --> 00:50:30,194
[Horseking] Now, the question is,
who ends up with one point?

955
00:50:30,277 --> 00:50:32,571
[Sanghyun] ZZONE has a chance,
and Junseo does too.

956
00:50:32,655 --> 00:50:33,781
[♪ tense music playing]

957
00:50:33,864 --> 00:50:35,783
[Horseking] It seems
Kim Ddolddol tagged ZZONE.

958
00:50:36,367 --> 00:50:38,536
-Ddolddol's at minus one anyway.
-[Horseking] Yeah.

959
00:50:38,619 --> 00:50:40,454
Then, it doesn't matter. It's good for us.

960
00:50:40,538 --> 00:50:41,872
What if ZZONE moves up?

961
00:50:41,956 --> 00:50:43,499
-After winning the battle?
-[Horseking] Yeah.

962
00:50:43,582 --> 00:50:45,084
Then, we should tag her first.

963
00:50:47,294 --> 00:50:48,587
[ZZONE] My head hurts.

964
00:50:51,048 --> 00:50:52,466
Did you have the battle?

965
00:50:52,550 --> 00:50:53,884
-[Horseking] Already?
-You already did it?

966
00:50:54,802 --> 00:50:56,971
-[ZZONE] I won.
-[Horseking exclaims]

967
00:50:57,054 --> 00:50:58,430
So you have one point now?

968
00:50:59,848 --> 00:51:02,601
TIED FOR 2ND
HORSEKING, SANGHYUN, ZZONE

969
00:51:03,227 --> 00:51:04,812
[Sanghyun] Now,
it's a fight among us three.

970
00:51:04,895 --> 00:51:07,106
I better get on the offensive quickly.

971
00:51:07,690 --> 00:51:10,276
I'd originally planned
to make all my moves towards the end,

972
00:51:10,359 --> 00:51:11,944
but I couldn't afford to wait.

973
00:51:15,197 --> 00:51:16,407
[Sanghyun] I better tag someone.

974
00:51:16,949 --> 00:51:18,450
[host] Tag confirmed.

975
00:51:18,534 --> 00:51:19,535
[Joonsu] No way!

976
00:51:19,618 --> 00:51:21,579
-[Horseking] What? You tagged him?
-[ZZONE] Yes.

977
00:51:22,162 --> 00:51:24,248
-[Sanghyun] Let's go.
-[Horseking] Who tagged first? Him?

978
00:51:24,331 --> 00:51:25,541
[ZZONE] I did.

979
00:51:26,208 --> 00:51:28,961
[Sanghyun] I thought, "What's going on?"
I was a little thrown off.

980
00:51:29,753 --> 00:51:31,922
Hold on, am I understanding
this situation right?

981
00:51:32,506 --> 00:51:33,716
Why did you tag me?

982
00:51:33,799 --> 00:51:35,175
[ZZONE] Because you were about to tag me.

983
00:51:35,259 --> 00:51:37,303
-Really?
-[ZZONE] Why were you going to tag me?

984
00:51:38,220 --> 00:51:39,680
[Sanghyun] Something felt a little off.

985
00:51:39,763 --> 00:51:42,975
ZZONE had come out
after just finishing a battle.

986
00:51:43,058 --> 00:51:45,936
There was no way
she still had any Weapon Cards.

987
00:51:53,068 --> 00:51:54,445
Did you only submit two cards?

988
00:52:02,244 --> 00:52:04,330
[dealer] Okay, both players
have submitted their cards.

989
00:52:05,039 --> 00:52:06,081
SANGHYUN'S CARD
MUTANT, 4

990
00:52:06,165 --> 00:52:07,207
[♪ exciting music playing]

991
00:52:07,291 --> 00:52:08,459
ZZONE'S CARD
COMMANDER, 5

992
00:52:09,335 --> 00:52:12,254
The winning player
may return to the chase area.

993
00:52:13,589 --> 00:52:15,215
Youn Sanghyun wins.

994
00:52:18,260 --> 00:52:20,763
[ZZONE] Sanghyun was trying
to attack first,

995
00:52:20,846 --> 00:52:22,598
so I thought he didn't have Defense cards.

996
00:52:23,390 --> 00:52:27,269
I only played the Commander,
the strongest Character Card.

997
00:52:27,978 --> 00:52:30,272
SHIELD, BARRICADE, MUTANT
COMMANDER

998
00:52:30,356 --> 00:52:31,440
TOTAL 9 POINTS
TOTAL 5 POINTS

999
00:52:31,523 --> 00:52:35,861
[Sanghyun] I had Defense cards,
so I was able to win.

1000
00:52:35,944 --> 00:52:39,573
I had a lot of coins,
so I didn't need to save my cards.

1001
00:52:40,407 --> 00:52:44,036
The first thing I bought at the Store
was the Secret Vault.

1002
00:52:46,246 --> 00:52:49,708
With the Secret Vault,
I could hold four Weapon Cards.

1003
00:52:51,627 --> 00:52:53,003
I'll take two Pistols.

1004
00:52:54,421 --> 00:52:57,174
I could still buy two more.

1005
00:52:57,257 --> 00:53:00,177
So, I'll buy a Shield and a Barricade.

1006
00:53:01,178 --> 00:53:04,348
Now that I have
both Attack and Defense cards,

1007
00:53:04,431 --> 00:53:08,227
I was 100% sure I could win every battle.

1008
00:53:08,310 --> 00:53:10,729
Now that I have two points,
I feel pretty safe.

1009
00:53:10,813 --> 00:53:12,648
TIED FOR 1ST JIMIN, SANGHYUN
2ND HORSEKING

1010
00:53:12,731 --> 00:53:13,899
TIED FOR 3RD JUNSEO, ZZONE

1011
00:53:15,275 --> 00:53:16,735
-[Sanghyun] ZZONE.
-[ZZONE] What is it?

1012
00:53:18,028 --> 00:53:19,530
It might be better to buy attack cards

1013
00:53:19,613 --> 00:53:20,906
-and tag people.
-[ZZONE] What?

1014
00:53:20,989 --> 00:53:22,991
Buying Attack cards
and tagging might be better.

1015
00:53:23,784 --> 00:53:25,619
We don't have much time left.

1016
00:53:26,370 --> 00:53:29,456
[ZZONE] How much time do we have?
20 minutes?

1017
00:53:29,540 --> 00:53:30,874
Damn, I'm in trouble.

1018
00:53:30,958 --> 00:53:35,212
I'm getting really anxious.
Time is running out in this round.

1019
00:53:35,295 --> 00:53:38,590
I don't have many coins,
so if I can't afford anything,

1020
00:53:38,674 --> 00:53:42,219
I'll sell my Character Cards
and buy Grenades to blow everyone up.

1021
00:53:43,387 --> 00:53:47,099
[players chatting indistinctly]

1022
00:53:47,182 --> 00:53:48,642
Can I tag you?

1023
00:53:48,726 --> 00:53:50,227
He said, "Can I tag you?"

1024
00:53:50,310 --> 00:53:52,438
I was running out of time,
so it was killing me.

1025
00:53:53,021 --> 00:53:55,399
For now, I needed to pretend
that I had some cards.

1026
00:53:55,482 --> 00:53:57,067
Want to battle? I'm all-in on defense.

1027
00:53:57,151 --> 00:54:00,529
You probably saw earlier.
I literally can't tag anyone.

1028
00:54:00,612 --> 00:54:01,613
Go ahead if you want.

1029
00:54:01,697 --> 00:54:02,781
ZZONE, JUNSEO
TIED FOR 3RD

1030
00:54:04,616 --> 00:54:05,743
[sighs]

1031
00:54:10,539 --> 00:54:12,082
Go ahead if you want.

1032
00:54:12,833 --> 00:54:14,877
-See? I only have Defense cards. Go ahead.
-Okay.

1033
00:54:14,960 --> 00:54:16,170
-Let's go.
-[host] Tag confirmed.

1034
00:54:16,253 --> 00:54:17,546
There's not much time left.

1035
00:54:18,630 --> 00:54:22,843
The longer I waited, the more I realized
this wasn't going anywhere.

1036
00:54:22,926 --> 00:54:26,889
So I went with a sure-fire strategy to win
and bought weapons this time.

1037
00:54:26,972 --> 00:54:29,183
A Pistol and a Wrench.

1038
00:54:30,684 --> 00:54:33,187
And then, I had to take someone out,

1039
00:54:33,270 --> 00:54:36,148
so I changed my approach
to become an Attacker.

1040
00:54:36,231 --> 00:54:38,066
JUNSEO SUBMITS HIS CARD

1041
00:54:38,150 --> 00:54:40,861
[dealer] Ms. ZZONE,
please submit your card.

1042
00:54:42,070 --> 00:54:44,072
ZZONE SUBMITS HER CARD

1043
00:54:44,156 --> 00:54:46,158
[ZZONE] It was basically all or nothing.

1044
00:54:47,034 --> 00:54:48,827
We'd been in a battle of wits
the whole time,

1045
00:54:48,911 --> 00:54:50,496
trying to figure each other out.

1046
00:54:51,121 --> 00:54:54,416
We had to read what people thought,
but it was impossible to know.

1047
00:54:55,292 --> 00:54:58,170
[dealer] We will reveal
the battle results.

1048
00:55:02,925 --> 00:55:04,718
ZZONE wins.

1049
00:55:04,801 --> 00:55:06,220
WINNER: ZZONE
LOSER: YUK JUNSEO

1050
00:55:06,803 --> 00:55:10,974
ZZONE, please take your cards first
and return to the chase area.

1051
00:55:11,058 --> 00:55:12,100
What did you play?

1052
00:55:12,184 --> 00:55:13,852
[♪ serious music playing]

1053
00:55:13,936 --> 00:55:16,146
What? I'm done. You can tell me now.

1054
00:55:16,688 --> 00:55:17,689
-You're done?
-[Junseo] Yeah.

1055
00:55:17,773 --> 00:55:19,483
-Come on. You still got this.
-[Junseo] What?

1056
00:55:19,566 --> 00:55:21,818
[ZZONE] You can do it. It's not over.

1057
00:55:23,153 --> 00:55:25,072
[Junseo sighs] I was angry.

1058
00:55:26,198 --> 00:55:27,908
Why did I lose?

1059
00:55:27,991 --> 00:55:31,245
I had a Wrench and a Pistol,

1060
00:55:31,328 --> 00:55:33,872
so there was no way
that combination could lose.

1061
00:55:33,956 --> 00:55:35,541
I had no idea why I lost.

1062
00:55:35,624 --> 00:55:36,792
COMMANDER, PISTOL, WRENCH

1063
00:55:37,501 --> 00:55:40,963
His play was actually pretty predictable.

1064
00:55:41,046 --> 00:55:44,132
Knowing Junseo,
he had played it very safe at first,

1065
00:55:44,216 --> 00:55:47,594
so I knew he'd use the Commander
in the final round.

1066
00:55:48,303 --> 00:55:50,389
So I played the Slave card.

1067
00:55:51,390 --> 00:55:53,517
I could always find a way to survive.

1068
00:55:53,600 --> 00:55:57,646
The point differential wasn't that big,
so I thought I could turn things around.

1069
00:55:57,729 --> 00:55:59,273
2ND ZZONE
3RD YUK JUNSEO

1070
00:55:59,356 --> 00:56:01,692
FIERCE BATTLE FOR THE TOP SPOTS

1071
00:56:01,775 --> 00:56:05,028
ONLY THE TOP THREE ADVANCE TO THE FINALS

1072
00:56:06,488 --> 00:56:07,489
[Horseking] How did it go?

1073
00:56:09,616 --> 00:56:10,659
-[Ddolddol] Who won?
-[Junseo] I lost.

1074
00:56:11,618 --> 00:56:12,869
[Ddolddol] Yuk Junseo versus ZZONE.

1075
00:56:12,953 --> 00:56:14,955
Gosh, ZZONE's climbing up the rankings.

1076
00:56:15,038 --> 00:56:16,206
[♪ contemplative music playing]

1077
00:56:16,290 --> 00:56:18,709
[Horseking] I had one point,

1078
00:56:19,501 --> 00:56:23,630
so I started to think
I could actually lose if I messed this up.

1079
00:56:26,508 --> 00:56:27,509
Want to battle?

1080
00:56:28,510 --> 00:56:29,511
No pressure.

1081
00:56:30,095 --> 00:56:31,847
I'm going to use a Smoke Bomb.

1082
00:56:31,930 --> 00:56:33,640
-A Smoke Bomb?
-You can if you want.

1083
00:56:33,724 --> 00:56:36,018
I only have Smoke Bombs.

1084
00:56:36,101 --> 00:56:37,561
SMOKE BOMB NULLIFIES THE BATTLE

1085
00:56:37,644 --> 00:56:40,105
[Horseking] I know I need
to start earning some points now.

1086
00:56:40,731 --> 00:56:42,357
I'll take one Smoke Bomb.

1087
00:56:43,609 --> 00:56:46,820
But I spent everything I had
on Smoke Bombs to stay at one point.

1088
00:56:48,071 --> 00:56:50,198
There was nothing I could do
with just Smoke Bombs.

1089
00:56:50,282 --> 00:56:52,034
I was so frustrated.

1090
00:56:52,117 --> 00:56:53,702
I was losing my mind.

1091
00:56:56,788 --> 00:56:57,789
What should I do?

1092
00:57:01,084 --> 00:57:02,878
-Want to battle?
-[Horseking] ZZONE... What?

1093
00:57:02,961 --> 00:57:04,046
-Let's battle.
-[Horseking] You want to?

1094
00:57:04,129 --> 00:57:05,130
All right.

1095
00:57:05,213 --> 00:57:06,423
[host] Tag confirmed.

1096
00:57:06,506 --> 00:57:07,924
[Horseking] I have two Smoke Bombs.

1097
00:57:08,008 --> 00:57:11,470
[dealer] The cards have been submitted.
We will check who the winner is.

1098
00:57:11,553 --> 00:57:14,848
-This battle has been nullified.
-[♪ serious music playing]

1099
00:57:16,391 --> 00:57:18,810
SLAVE
SMOKE BOMB, MUTANT

1100
00:57:18,894 --> 00:57:21,772
HORSEKING USES SMOKE BOMB

1101
00:57:21,855 --> 00:57:25,150
Once you use a Smoke Bomb,
everything gets nullified.

1102
00:57:25,233 --> 00:57:26,360
It cancels the battle.

1103
00:57:26,443 --> 00:57:29,946
I couldn't earn any points,
so that was really disappointing.

1104
00:57:31,281 --> 00:57:34,743
[Horseking] Because of those Smoke Bombs,
I got rid of all my Attack cards.

1105
00:57:34,826 --> 00:57:37,496
[sighs] Time kept ticking away,

1106
00:57:37,579 --> 00:57:40,540
and I realized
I was running low on coins too.

1107
00:57:40,624 --> 00:57:43,126
That's when my mind went totally blank.

1108
00:57:44,336 --> 00:57:46,213
I just went...

1109
00:57:47,631 --> 00:57:49,424
ZZONE TAGGED SANGHYUN
ZZONE TAGGED HORSEKING

1110
00:57:49,508 --> 00:57:50,884
As I watched the tagging situation,

1111
00:57:50,967 --> 00:57:53,637
I knew ZZONE or Sanghyun
would climb the rankings.

1112
00:57:54,680 --> 00:57:56,098
But all I had were Smoke Bombs,

1113
00:57:56,181 --> 00:57:58,392
so I could only hide,
and it made me anxious.

1114
00:58:01,144 --> 00:58:04,314
My usual style
is to attack and earn points.

1115
00:58:04,398 --> 00:58:07,150
And if I fail, it's fine.
I can play and earn points again.

1116
00:58:09,277 --> 00:58:12,322
As a player, I always want
to give it my all and be professional.

1117
00:58:19,121 --> 00:58:20,747
I'd come all this way,

1118
00:58:21,915 --> 00:58:23,875
and I was just one step away
from the finals.

1119
00:58:24,501 --> 00:58:29,297
But there wasn't much time left.
I had no money, no cards, and no options.

1120
00:58:29,381 --> 00:58:30,382
This is driving me crazy.

1121
00:58:31,174 --> 00:58:32,217
This is hard.

1122
00:58:34,594 --> 00:58:35,971
[sighs heavily]

1123
00:58:36,930 --> 00:58:41,977
I realized I'd completely miscalculated,
and at that point...

1124
00:58:42,060 --> 00:58:43,437
I was so frustrated!

1125
00:58:43,520 --> 00:58:46,773
I was supposed to be playing the game,
but I couldn't do anything.

1126
00:58:48,984 --> 00:58:50,235
What's wrong with me?

1127
00:58:53,488 --> 00:58:55,699
Did I focus too much on just defense?

1128
00:58:55,782 --> 00:58:57,534
All kinds of thoughts ran through my head.

1129
00:58:59,119 --> 00:59:00,662
[sighs]

1130
00:59:03,832 --> 00:59:06,793
And the whole time,
I kept looking at my watch.

1131
00:59:06,877 --> 00:59:09,004
I was basically hoping
the game would just end.

1132
00:59:12,215 --> 00:59:18,263
HORSEKING KEPT CHECKING HIS WATCH
THROUGHOUT ROUND 2

1133
00:59:21,349 --> 00:59:24,895
When I saw myself hiding
and just hoping for the end to come,

1134
00:59:24,978 --> 00:59:26,938
it suddenly hit me really hard.

1135
00:59:31,526 --> 00:59:34,070
I was disgusted with myself.

1136
00:59:46,833 --> 00:59:51,630
HORSEKING SMASHES HIS WATCH

1137
00:59:53,131 --> 00:59:56,009
10 MINUTES BEFORE GAME ENDS

1138
00:59:58,595 --> 01:00:01,431
I'd made it this far without giving up.

1139
01:00:03,475 --> 01:00:06,102
I couldn't run away anymore.
I started moving around again.

1140
01:00:06,186 --> 01:00:08,104
I reset my goal.

1141
01:00:09,689 --> 01:00:11,608
It isn't over until it's over.

1142
01:00:15,028 --> 01:00:16,154
[exclaims, laughs]

1143
01:00:16,238 --> 01:00:17,739
[coins jiggle]

1144
01:00:19,741 --> 01:00:22,410
I thought,
"Let's settle this once and for all."

1145
01:00:22,494 --> 01:00:23,495
All right.

1146
01:00:24,579 --> 01:00:25,580
Whatever.

1147
01:00:27,332 --> 01:00:29,835
If I use a First Aid Kit,
I can save a card, right?

1148
01:00:31,002 --> 01:00:32,003
One Soldier...

1149
01:00:32,087 --> 01:00:33,672
RECOVER ONE ELIMINATED CHARACTER CARD

1150
01:00:33,755 --> 01:00:34,756
I'd like that, please.

1151
01:00:35,423 --> 01:00:37,884
I'll sell my Citizen, Soldier,
and Commander cards.

1152
01:00:37,968 --> 01:00:38,969
CARDS PREVIOUSLY SOLD

1153
01:00:39,052 --> 01:00:40,554
I'll sell these three cards.

1154
01:00:40,637 --> 01:00:42,514
FIRST AID KIT USED
SOLDIER CARD RECOVERED

1155
01:00:43,348 --> 01:00:45,058
I'll take one Pistol.

1156
01:00:45,141 --> 01:00:46,476
It's all or nothing now.

1157
01:00:46,560 --> 01:00:51,147
SMOKE BOMB, PISTOL

1158
01:00:52,023 --> 01:00:53,024
[sniffs]

1159
01:00:57,529 --> 01:00:58,989
How many points does he have?

1160
01:00:59,072 --> 01:01:01,741
Who? Joonsu? He's at minus three now.

1161
01:01:02,784 --> 01:01:03,910
He only attacked.

1162
01:01:06,413 --> 01:01:07,497
Wait a minute.

1163
01:01:08,790 --> 01:01:11,334
I realized I could
at least take Joonsu out.

1164
01:01:12,794 --> 01:01:14,379
-[host] Tag confirmed.
-Okay.

1165
01:01:15,255 --> 01:01:16,298
He tagged him.

1166
01:01:16,381 --> 01:01:20,343
[Horseking] I thought I needed to attack
someone too, so I went after Joonsu.

1167
01:01:20,844 --> 01:01:23,013
[dealer] Mr. Horseking,
please submit your card face down.

1168
01:01:23,096 --> 01:01:24,222
HORSEKING
RANKING: 2, SCORE: 1

1169
01:01:24,306 --> 01:01:26,391
Mr. Lee Joonsu,
please submit your card as well.

1170
01:01:28,852 --> 01:01:30,437
We will announce the results.

1171
01:01:30,520 --> 01:01:31,605
SOLDIER, PISTOL
SLAVE

1172
01:01:33,231 --> 01:01:36,026
TOTAL 6 POINTS
TOTAL 2 POINTS

1173
01:01:36,651 --> 01:01:39,112
The winner is Horseking.

1174
01:01:40,280 --> 01:01:44,451
I thought, "There's no way I'm losing
a Death Match that leads to the finals."

1175
01:01:44,534 --> 01:01:46,786
So, I had to win this.

1176
01:01:46,870 --> 01:01:48,997
I thought, "I have to advance."

1177
01:01:49,080 --> 01:01:50,165
2ND HORSEKING

1178
01:01:50,248 --> 01:01:53,335
1ST HORSEKING, 2 POINTS

1179
01:01:54,961 --> 01:01:57,547
5 MINUTES BEFORE GAME ENDS

1180
01:01:57,631 --> 01:01:58,965
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1181
01:02:00,050 --> 01:02:01,259
2 COINS

1182
01:02:01,343 --> 01:02:04,930
1ST HORSEKING, 2 POINTS

1183
01:02:07,849 --> 01:02:10,352
[Sanghyun] I need to beat ZZONE
and end this once and for all.

1184
01:02:11,269 --> 01:02:13,188
Everyone was close in points,
so I was nervous.

1185
01:02:13,271 --> 01:02:15,523
I felt like I needed to make
a decisive move.

1186
01:02:17,150 --> 01:02:23,281
1ST YOUN SANGHYUN, 2 POINTS

1187
01:02:26,785 --> 01:02:29,245
1ST PARK JIMIN, 2 POINTS

1188
01:02:31,289 --> 01:02:34,376
2ND ZZONE, 1 POINT

1189
01:02:34,459 --> 01:02:37,504
ZZONE WILL MISS THE FINALS AT THIS RATE

1190
01:02:37,587 --> 01:02:41,466
[ZZONE] Offense has more of an advantage
in this game, so I needed to attack.

1191
01:02:42,092 --> 01:02:46,346
TIED FOR 1ST: HORSEKING, SANGHYUN, JIMIN
2ND: ZZONE

1192
01:02:47,514 --> 01:02:49,015
Hello.

1193
01:02:51,267 --> 01:02:54,062
We were running out of time,
so I sold my Character Cards.

1194
01:02:54,145 --> 01:02:55,438
[♪ contemplative music playing]

1195
01:02:57,440 --> 01:02:59,359
I decided to go all-in on attacking.

1196
01:03:01,736 --> 01:03:05,073
Jimin was actually my target.

1197
01:03:05,156 --> 01:03:06,992
She's completely vanished.

1198
01:03:07,075 --> 01:03:10,412
The round was almost over,
and I couldn't see her anywhere.

1199
01:03:10,912 --> 01:03:12,539
I need to find her fast.

1200
01:03:15,375 --> 01:03:16,376
[Jimin whispers] Darn it, Horseking.

1201
01:03:21,089 --> 01:03:23,508
[Jimin] I was hiding, so I didn't know
how the game was going.

1202
01:03:23,591 --> 01:03:24,718
It was frustrating.

1203
01:03:27,220 --> 01:03:30,098
I thought I'd just go check
Horseking's score,

1204
01:03:30,181 --> 01:03:31,933
so I headed to the Store.

1205
01:03:42,986 --> 01:03:44,029
[exclaims in surprise]

1206
01:03:45,321 --> 01:03:46,865
[host] Tag confirmed.

1207
01:03:46,948 --> 01:03:49,826
She was getting closer,
so I thought, "Great," and I tagged her.

1208
01:03:49,909 --> 01:03:51,411
-[♪ suspenseful music playing]
-I wanted to win this and take the lead.

1209
01:03:51,494 --> 01:03:53,038
[dealer] Ms. ZZONE, as the Attacker,

1210
01:03:53,121 --> 01:03:54,581
-please submit your card.
-Okay.

1211
01:03:56,124 --> 01:03:58,501
[ZZONE] Jimin had been hiding
the whole time,

1212
01:03:59,002 --> 01:04:01,629
so I figured she wouldn't have
any coins or cards left.

1213
01:04:03,006 --> 01:04:05,216
[Jimin] The rankings will change
the moment you lose.

1214
01:04:06,801 --> 01:04:11,431
[host] Only one player from this battle
will advance to the finals.

1215
01:04:11,514 --> 01:04:13,475
[Jimin] If I win this battle,

1216
01:04:13,558 --> 01:04:16,519
I earn my ticket to the finals.

1217
01:04:18,646 --> 01:04:21,149
[dealer] Both players
have submitted their cards.

1218
01:04:21,733 --> 01:04:23,610
We will check who the winner is.

1219
01:04:23,693 --> 01:04:25,278
[♪ suspenseful music playing]

1220
01:04:31,618 --> 01:04:33,244
We will announce the battle results.

1221
01:04:34,454 --> 01:04:35,955
WRENCH, BASIC ATTACK CARD

1222
01:04:36,039 --> 01:04:37,457
SHIELD, BASIC DEFENSE CARD

1223
01:04:40,001 --> 01:04:41,127
The winner is...

1224
01:04:47,258 --> 01:04:48,301
[mic feedback]

1225
01:04:48,384 --> 01:04:50,386
[host] The game is over.

1226
01:04:51,596 --> 01:04:54,516
We will reveal the results of "Dystopia."

1227
01:04:54,599 --> 01:04:55,809
[♪ tense music playing]

1228
01:04:55,892 --> 01:04:57,727
The additional finalists are...

1229
01:05:04,275 --> 01:05:05,443
Youn Sanghyun,

1230
01:05:06,319 --> 01:05:07,320
Horseking,

1231
01:05:08,154 --> 01:05:09,239
and...

1232
01:05:15,161 --> 01:05:16,663
-Park Jimin.
-[♪ triumphant music playing]

1233
01:05:16,746 --> 01:05:18,081
PARK JIMIN: 3 POINTS

1234
01:05:18,164 --> 01:05:21,251
[Jimin] Luckily, ZZONE tagged me first,

1235
01:05:21,334 --> 01:05:23,628
-so I was the Defender.
-[ZZONE] Why did you let me tag you?

1236
01:05:23,711 --> 01:05:27,298
I had been waiting to get tagged.

1237
01:05:27,382 --> 01:05:29,217
I had quite a few Defense cards.

1238
01:05:29,300 --> 01:05:31,636
SHIELD, BULLETPROOF VEST,
BULLETPROOF VEST

1239
01:05:33,847 --> 01:05:35,140
[dealer] We will check who the winner is.

1240
01:05:35,223 --> 01:05:36,933
JIMIN'S CARDS
MUTANT 4, SHIELD 1

1241
01:05:37,016 --> 01:05:38,184
PAIR OF BULLETPROOF VESTS 4

1242
01:05:38,685 --> 01:05:41,604
PARK JIMIN
TOTAL 9 POINTS

1243
01:05:42,188 --> 01:05:43,648
COMMANDER, SOLDIER, WRENCH, PISTOL

1244
01:05:43,731 --> 01:05:46,109
ZZONE REVIVES COMMANDER
AND ITS HIGHEST ATTACK STAT

1245
01:05:46,192 --> 01:05:50,071
SPECIAL CONDITION BENEFIT
MAXIMUM ATTACK STAT OF 9

1246
01:05:51,823 --> 01:05:54,826
[ZZONE] If I just win this battle,
I'd advance to the finals.

1247
01:05:56,494 --> 01:05:58,580
WRENCH, PISTOL

1248
01:05:58,663 --> 01:06:00,248
8 ATTACK POINTS
BUT ZZONE PLAYED SOLDIER

1249
01:06:00,331 --> 01:06:02,709
[dealer] The winner is Park Jimin.

1250
01:06:02,792 --> 01:06:05,545
[ZZONE] If Jimin plays the Slave
by any chance,

1251
01:06:05,628 --> 01:06:07,630
all of this would be for nothing.

1252
01:06:07,714 --> 01:06:09,799
So, it was hard for me
to play the Commander.

1253
01:06:11,050 --> 01:06:13,553
MUTANT, SHIELD, 2 BULLETPROOF VESTS
JIMIN: TOTAL 9 POINTS

1254
01:06:13,636 --> 01:06:15,930
SOLDIER, WRENCH, PISTOL
ZZONE: TOTAL 8 POINTS

1255
01:06:16,014 --> 01:06:17,015
Thank you.

1256
01:06:17,098 --> 01:06:18,683
[ZZONE] Weren't you going to use
a Smoke Bomb?

1257
01:06:19,642 --> 01:06:20,977
[sighs]

1258
01:06:21,060 --> 01:06:24,522
Gosh, if I'd just tried a little harder,

1259
01:06:24,606 --> 01:06:26,649
I could've made it to the finals.

1260
01:06:26,733 --> 01:06:28,818
I was so close. It's such a bummer.

1261
01:06:29,861 --> 01:06:31,029
1ST PARK JIMIN
2ND ZZONE

1262
01:06:31,112 --> 01:06:34,866
1ST PARK JIMIN
2ND HORSEKING, YOUN SANGHYUN

1263
01:06:34,949 --> 01:06:36,117
[♪ exciting music playing]

1264
01:06:36,201 --> 01:06:38,703
[Sanghyun]
I've never actually lost a game before,

1265
01:06:38,786 --> 01:06:42,665
so it made me think,
"I guess I'm playing this pretty well."

1266
01:06:42,749 --> 01:06:44,667
Jimin is really good
at these type of games.

1267
01:06:44,751 --> 01:06:49,964
I'm the one who earned three points
with skill in head-to-head battles.

1268
01:06:50,757 --> 01:06:52,884
This time, I won by playing aggressively

1269
01:06:52,967 --> 01:06:54,844
and using my strength
of outsmarting people.

1270
01:06:54,928 --> 01:06:58,473
The true winner of "Dystopia"
is Park Jimin.

1271
01:06:58,556 --> 01:07:00,725
[Horseking]
I made such a huge mistake this time

1272
01:07:00,808 --> 01:07:03,228
that I was more angry at myself
than happy about winning.

1273
01:07:03,311 --> 01:07:06,064
I was pretty disgusted with myself then.

1274
01:07:06,147 --> 01:07:08,608
But since I still made it through,

1275
01:07:08,691 --> 01:07:11,194
I decided I was going to
do things my way in the finals.

1276
01:07:11,277 --> 01:07:14,030
[host] Excluding
the three additional finalists,

1277
01:07:14,113 --> 01:07:16,783
-[♪ sad music playing]
-Kim Ddolddol, ZZONE,

1278
01:07:16,866 --> 01:07:19,827
Yuk Junseo, and Lee Joonsu,

1279
01:07:19,911 --> 01:07:22,455
please exit the area immediately.

1280
01:07:23,081 --> 01:07:25,333
Eliminated players
will not be able to return

1281
01:07:25,416 --> 01:07:26,417
-to Deadly Tag.
-[Ddolddol] Good job.

1282
01:07:26,542 --> 01:07:27,710
-[Joonsu] Good work.
-[ZZONE] You did great.

1283
01:07:27,794 --> 01:07:28,795
[Jaegyun] You did great.

1284
01:07:28,878 --> 01:07:29,921
-Let's meet up later.
-Sure.

1285
01:07:30,004 --> 01:07:31,589
-That was fun.
-It really was.

1286
01:07:32,173 --> 01:07:33,258
[sighs]

1287
01:07:33,341 --> 01:07:35,677
[Ddolddol] Not making it to the finals
is disappointing.

1288
01:07:35,760 --> 01:07:39,597
But I had so much fun playing these games.

1289
01:07:39,681 --> 01:07:40,932
An alcoholic.

1290
01:07:41,015 --> 01:07:43,726
I played almost every game,
including the Death Match.

1291
01:07:45,019 --> 01:07:47,272
And I always fought
my way back from the brink.

1292
01:07:49,357 --> 01:07:52,068
It's getting pretty annoying
to be named twice.

1293
01:07:52,151 --> 01:07:54,612
No one played Deadly Tag
as intensely as I did.

1294
01:07:54,696 --> 01:07:56,739
Maybe I'll start cleaning.

1295
01:07:56,823 --> 01:07:58,700
Even if we lose, let's lose in style.

1296
01:07:58,783 --> 01:08:00,410
DDOLDDOL ENJOYED PLAYING
MORE THAN ANYONE

1297
01:08:00,493 --> 01:08:01,661
If I catch you, you're dead.

1298
01:08:02,537 --> 01:08:03,871
This is a battle of wits.

1299
01:08:04,956 --> 01:08:05,957
Hey, you...

1300
01:08:06,040 --> 01:08:09,002
It was called a Death Match,
but it basically was the semi-finals.

1301
01:08:09,085 --> 01:08:11,212
Me? I did better than I thought.

1302
01:08:12,463 --> 01:08:14,257
[Sanghyun] Joonsu, see you on the outside.

1303
01:08:14,340 --> 01:08:15,425
-[Joonsu] At school?
-[Sanghyun] On the outside.

1304
01:08:15,508 --> 01:08:17,427
See you on the outside.
We'll hang out more.

1305
01:08:19,053 --> 01:08:23,224
[Joonsu] I've always shown
my cheerful side on TV,

1306
01:08:23,308 --> 01:08:26,769
but I wanted to show
that I had skills to betray people too.

1307
01:08:27,687 --> 01:08:29,564
[Jaegyun] Hey, Joonsu tagged me twice.

1308
01:08:31,858 --> 01:08:37,655
JOONSU SHOWED
A NEW SIDE OF HIMSELF TO SURVIVE

1309
01:08:37,739 --> 01:08:39,991
Hey. They took my notebook.

1310
01:08:40,074 --> 01:08:41,409
Even if I got eliminated,

1311
01:08:41,492 --> 01:08:45,913
I wanted to have fun, enjoy every moment,
and leave without regrets.

1312
01:08:46,497 --> 01:08:49,250
I wanted to betray people
and show a ruthless side of myself.

1313
01:08:49,334 --> 01:08:50,585
Can't you let me go one time?

1314
01:08:51,294 --> 01:08:52,712
Horseking, let's go talk.

1315
01:08:54,047 --> 01:08:55,298
Can you help me out just once?

1316
01:08:55,798 --> 01:08:57,133
"I just need to be having fun."

1317
01:08:57,216 --> 01:08:59,927
With this mindset, I went completely wild.

1318
01:09:00,011 --> 01:09:01,012
I had a lot of fun.

1319
01:09:01,679 --> 01:09:03,556
Good job. Good luck!

1320
01:09:04,098 --> 01:09:05,892
-[Dail] You did well.
-[ZZONE] Good luck in the final!

1321
01:09:05,975 --> 01:09:07,810
I was actually hoping
you'd make it, ZZONE.

1322
01:09:07,894 --> 01:09:10,229
[ZZONE] That old saying really is true.

1323
01:09:10,313 --> 01:09:13,274
"Even if a tiger takes you away,
you'll live if you keep your wits."

1324
01:09:13,358 --> 01:09:15,610
It felt like
everyone around me were tigers.

1325
01:09:16,444 --> 01:09:18,780
[ZZONE exclaims, laughs]

1326
01:09:19,864 --> 01:09:22,116
Wait!

1327
01:09:22,200 --> 01:09:24,577
But as long as I kept my head here,

1328
01:09:24,660 --> 01:09:27,789
there was always a way
to solve problems and win.

1329
01:09:27,872 --> 01:09:29,791
Seriously, I'm not lying!

1330
01:09:29,874 --> 01:09:32,085
I'll head to the Death Match and pick you.

1331
01:09:32,168 --> 01:09:33,878
They don't know who it is,
so what can they do?

1332
01:09:33,961 --> 01:09:36,547
-We'd be almost invincible.
-Isn't this a guaranteed win?

1333
01:09:36,631 --> 01:09:37,924
FOUND HER OWN WAY TO SURVIVE

1334
01:09:38,007 --> 01:09:40,843
By the later stages,
I was able to be more steady

1335
01:09:40,927 --> 01:09:41,928
"ZZONE FOUGHT HARD"

1336
01:09:42,011 --> 01:09:44,639
and play without being intimidated.

1337
01:09:44,722 --> 01:09:46,641
-It's over!
-[Ddolddol] Were you the Joker?

1338
01:09:46,724 --> 01:09:50,144
I learned that in life,
it's all about confidence.

1339
01:09:50,728 --> 01:09:52,480
Hey, Junseo. You did amazing.

1340
01:09:52,563 --> 01:09:54,482
It was an honor to have played with you.

1341
01:09:54,565 --> 01:09:56,401
You did great. Seriously.

1342
01:09:57,235 --> 01:10:00,530
[Junseo sighs] I was very sad
and disappointed.

1343
01:10:01,072 --> 01:10:02,281
[both grunting]

1344
01:10:02,365 --> 01:10:04,492
I genuinely played hard.
I wanted to win so badly.

1345
01:10:05,576 --> 01:10:07,245
JUNSEO WAS THE MOST IMMERSED IN THE GAME

1346
01:10:07,328 --> 01:10:08,371
[Junseo] Hey! Tag, tag.

1347
01:10:08,454 --> 01:10:10,456
-[Jieun grunting]
-I'm sorry.

1348
01:10:10,540 --> 01:10:12,834
If you confuse me,
I'll accuse you of being the Seeker.

1349
01:10:12,917 --> 01:10:15,211
It's just us. Why can't you talk?

1350
01:10:17,171 --> 01:10:24,137
AFTER END OF DEATH MATCH

1351
01:10:37,316 --> 01:10:38,609
[sniffles]

1352
01:10:40,945 --> 01:10:42,947
[sniffles]

1353
01:10:45,408 --> 01:10:46,659
[sniffles]

1354
01:10:48,703 --> 01:10:50,955
I ended up crying after it was over.

1355
01:10:51,038 --> 01:10:52,165
[♪ moody music playing]

1356
01:10:52,248 --> 01:10:54,459
I kept thinking
about all those crucial moments

1357
01:10:54,542 --> 01:10:57,628
when I could've easily advanced.

1358
01:10:59,964 --> 01:11:04,177
I had regrets and kept thinking,
"I should've played smarter."

1359
01:11:04,260 --> 01:11:06,137
I won't. I'm white, but I won't tag you.

1360
01:11:07,472 --> 01:11:12,059
Deadly Tag was one
of the toughest programs I've ever done,

1361
01:11:12,143 --> 01:11:14,562
but it was also one where I learned a lot.

1362
01:11:15,146 --> 01:11:18,107
I don't know where else
I'd ever get an experience like this.

1363
01:11:19,442 --> 01:11:20,651
[Ddolddol] "I want to survive."

1364
01:11:20,735 --> 01:11:23,863
I wonder if I'll ever feel
that type of emotion again.

1365
01:11:24,822 --> 01:11:27,575
It felt like
I'd stepped into another world.

1366
01:11:28,785 --> 01:11:31,412
It was like I had this long dream
for a week and woke up.

1367
01:11:32,330 --> 01:11:35,082
When I return home, I feel like

1368
01:11:35,708 --> 01:11:38,169
I'll be able to throw myself
into whatever I do.

1369
01:11:40,505 --> 01:11:42,131
[Dail] Seriously,

1370
01:11:42,215 --> 01:11:45,343
all the people
I thought would be the toughest to beat

1371
01:11:45,426 --> 01:11:47,303
made the finals. [chuckles]

1372
01:11:47,386 --> 01:11:48,721
[♪ tense music playing]

1373
01:11:54,310 --> 01:11:56,187
[mic feedback]

1374
01:11:56,270 --> 01:11:58,648
[host] The five finalists
have been determined

1375
01:11:58,731 --> 01:12:02,193
to decide the winner of Deadly Tag.

1376
01:12:03,277 --> 01:12:08,950
Yang Dail, Hwang Jaegyun, Park Jimin,
Youn Sanghyun, and Horseking.

1377
01:12:09,617 --> 01:12:12,203
In this most primal dog-eat-dog world,

1378
01:12:12,286 --> 01:12:16,332
we hope you survive to the very end
and become the last one standing.

1379
01:12:17,667 --> 01:12:21,003
[Jaegyun] Looking at the physical matchups
in this group,

1380
01:12:21,087 --> 01:12:22,421
I think I could win.

1381
01:12:22,505 --> 01:12:26,050
[Jimin] The games we'd played so far
didn't solely rely on athleticism,

1382
01:12:26,133 --> 01:12:28,427
so I thought I had a good shot at winning.

1383
01:12:29,095 --> 01:12:32,223
[Dail] There were definitely people
I was wary of in terms of athleticism,

1384
01:12:32,306 --> 01:12:33,933
but I was more concerned about Sanghyun.

1385
01:12:34,016 --> 01:12:35,142
[Sanghyun] He's really quick

1386
01:12:35,226 --> 01:12:37,562
at figuring out the key
to winning each game.

1387
01:12:38,771 --> 01:12:41,774
Since he's both physically strong
and good at using his brain,

1388
01:12:41,858 --> 01:12:43,901
Horseking was the one I was most wary of.

1389
01:12:43,985 --> 01:12:46,487
But I'm younger than him,
so I was confident.

1390
01:12:47,780 --> 01:12:49,657
[Horseking] Whatever game it is,
I'm going to be attacking.

1391
01:12:49,740 --> 01:12:52,159
I'll just completely overwhelm everyone.

1392
01:12:54,579 --> 01:12:55,746
[♪ thrilling music playing]

1393
01:12:55,830 --> 01:12:56,998
[explosion]

1394
01:12:58,958 --> 01:13:00,084
[players exclaim]

1395
01:13:01,043 --> 01:13:02,461
[Horseking] I'm a Good Citizen.

1396
01:13:03,379 --> 01:13:04,380
Stop!

1397
01:13:05,423 --> 01:13:08,050
6 DAYS TO GO

1398
01:13:08,134 --> 01:13:09,844
[Horseking] It's okay, get up. Okay.

1399
01:13:09,927 --> 01:13:11,387
-[Jimin] Watch out!
-[Ddolddol] Be careful!

1400
01:13:11,470 --> 01:13:13,055
[players cheer]

1401
01:13:13,139 --> 01:13:14,515
[Pani Bottle] We put up
a really good fight.

1402
01:13:14,599 --> 01:13:15,808
2 DAYS TO GO

1403
01:13:15,892 --> 01:13:16,934
1 DAY TO GO

1404
01:13:17,018 --> 01:13:18,227
[players exclaim]

1405
01:13:18,311 --> 01:13:20,354
[players clapping]

1406
01:13:20,438 --> 01:13:22,648
THE DAY IS HERE

1407
01:13:23,900 --> 01:13:25,109
[host] Deadly Tag.

1408
01:13:25,192 --> 01:13:27,612
We will reveal the final game.

1409
01:13:29,196 --> 01:13:31,198
[♪ ominous music playing]

1410
01:13:51,177 --> 01:13:53,179
Translated by Youji Kim
